    {
      "type": 12,
      "conditionalVisibility": {
        "parameterName": "selectedTab",
        "comparison": "isEqualTo",
        "value": "copilot"
      },
      "content": {
        "version": "NotebookGroup/1.0",
        "groupType": "editable",
        "items": [
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "## 🟦 Microsoft 365 Copilot — CopilotActivity\n\nReads the **CopilotActivity** table (Microsoft Copilot connector). LLMEventData carries prompts, responses, accessed resources, RAG sources, and per-message jailbreak / XPIA flags.\n\n**How to read this tab:** start with interaction volume and active agents, then pivot from an unusual agent or actor into the jailbreak/XPIA event lists and grounding-site inventory. Counts represent audit records, not necessarily unique prompts, successful attacks, or completed actions. `JailbreakDetected` is a direct user-prompt attack signal; `XPIADetected` identifies potentially malicious instructions in content the copilot accessed. A flag means the control detected risk, not that the model followed the instruction. Prompt, response, and resource metadata depend on Microsoft 365 audit licensing, connector configuration, and service schema population.",
              "style": "info"
            },
            "name": "cp-h"
          },
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "#### M365 Copilot coverage and risk counters\n\n`Interactions` counts `CopilotInteraction` audit records; distinct agents and actors count populated IDs or names across the selected period. Jailbreak and XPIA values count expanded message or resource elements carrying Microsoft detection flags, while plugin/config counts cover every non-interaction `RecordType`. These measures have different grains and must not be added together as a total workload or incident count."
            },
            "name": "cp-kpi-desc"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "union isfuzzy=true\r\n(CopilotActivity | where RecordType == 'CopilotInteraction' | summarize Value = count() | extend Metric = 'Interactions', Order = 1),\r\n(CopilotActivity | summarize Value = dcount(AgentId) | extend Metric = 'Distinct agents', Order = 2),\r\n(CopilotActivity | summarize Value = dcount(ActorName) | extend Metric = 'Distinct actors', Order = 3),\r\n(CopilotActivity | where RecordType == 'CopilotInteraction' | mv-expand m = LLMEventData.Messages | where tobool(m.JailbreakDetected) == true | summarize Value = count() | extend Metric = 'Jailbreak-flagged', Order = 4),\r\n(CopilotActivity | where RecordType == 'CopilotInteraction' | mv-expand r = LLMEventData.AccessedResources | where tobool(r.XPIADetected) == true | summarize Value = count() | extend Metric = 'XPIA (indirect inj.)', Order = 5),\r\n(CopilotActivity | where RecordType != 'CopilotInteraction' | summarize Value = count() | extend Metric = 'Plugin/config events', Order = 6)\r\n| project Order, Metric, Value\r\n| sort by Order asc",
              "size": 3,
              "visualization": "tiles",
              "title": "M365 Copilot metrics",
              "tileSettings": {
                "leftContent": {
                  "columnMatch": "Value",
                  "formatter": 12,
                  "formatOptions": {
                    "palette": "blue"
                  }
                },
                "showBorder": true,
                "titleContent": {
                  "columnMatch": "Metric",
                  "formatter": 1
                }
              },
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{Workspace}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "cp-kpi"
          },
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "#### Interaction and administration trend\n\nThis chart groups every `CopilotActivity` record by hour and `RecordType`. Use it to distinguish end-user interaction growth from agent, plugin, prompt-book, or settings changes and to align a spike with a deployment or incident window. Audit ingestion delay and low-volume record types can make the most recent bucket incomplete."
            },
            "name": "cp-time-desc"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "CopilotActivity\r\n| summarize Events = count() by bin(TimeGenerated, 1h), RecordType",
              "size": 0,
              "visualization": "timechart",
              "title": "Interactions vs config events over time (RecordType)",
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{Workspace}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "cp-time"
          },
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "#### Top agents by interactions\n\nThis ranks agents by `CopilotInteraction` audit records and adds distinct actors plus last-seen time. High volume can mean successful adoption, scheduled or automated usage, broad assignment, or a runaway workflow; it is not a count of unique conversations or successful answers. Compare `Actors` and `LastSeen`, apply the agent or actor filter, then pivot to XPIA, jailbreak, grounding resources, and configuration events before treating concentration as suspicious."
            },
            "name": "cp-agents-desc"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "CopilotActivity\r\n| where RecordType == 'CopilotInteraction'\r\n| where '{AgentSearch}' == '' or AgentName has '{AgentSearch}' or ActorName has '{AgentSearch}'\r\n| summarize Interactions = count(), Actors = dcount(ActorName), LastSeen = max(TimeGenerated) by AgentName, AgentId\r\n| top 25 by Interactions desc",
              "size": 0,
              "title": "Top agents by interactions",
              "gridSettings": {
                "formatters": [
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "Interactions",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "blue"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{Workspace}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "cp-agents"
          },
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "### 🚨 Jailbreak & indirect prompt injection (XPIA)\n\nA **direct user-prompt attack** (historically called a jailbreak) is typed by a user to override or evade system instructions. **XPIA**, or indirect prompt injection, places malicious instructions in content the copilot retrieves, such as documents, email, pages, or other grounding data. Microsoft detection flags are high-value triage signals, but a flag does not show whether the content was blocked, the model followed it, or a tool performed an action. Investigate the actor, agent, conversation, source resource, resulting response/tool activity, and related alerts."
            },
            "name": "cp-h2"
          },
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "#### Direct user-prompt attack detections\n\nA row appears when a message element has `JailbreakDetected == true`, Microsoft's direct prompt-attack signal for attempts to override or evade the copilot's instructions. The flag shows detection, not whether the attempt succeeded or an action executed. Investigate repeated actors, conversation and message IDs, the agent's permissions and tools, downstream actions, and related alerts; retain prompt content only under approved investigation controls."
            },
            "name": "cp-jb-desc"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "CopilotActivity\r\n| where RecordType == 'CopilotInteraction'\r\n| mv-expand m = LLMEventData.Messages\r\n| where tobool(m.JailbreakDetected) == true\r\n| where '{AgentSearch}' == '' or AgentName has '{AgentSearch}' or ActorName has '{AgentSearch}'\n| project TimeGenerated, ThreatLevel = '🔴 Jailbreak', AgentName, ActorName, ConversationId = tostring(LLMEventData.ConversationId), MessageId = tostring(m.Id)\r\n| order by TimeGenerated desc\r\n| take 100",
              "size": 0,
              "title": "Jailbreak-flagged messages",
              "gridSettings": {
                "formatters": [
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "ThreatLevel",
                    "formatter": 0
                  }
                ]
              },
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{Workspace}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "cp-jb"
          },
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "#### Indirect prompt injection on grounding content\n\nXPIA occurs when malicious instructions are embedded in content the copilot retrieves rather than typed directly by the user. This grid expands accessed resources with `XPIADetected == true`; `SiteUrl`, `Type`, and `Action` identify the source and access context. Detection does not prove the instruction influenced the model, so verify the resource, resulting response or tool activity, data exposure, and whether access should be revoked or the content quarantined."
            },
            "name": "cp-xpia-desc"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "CopilotActivity\r\n| where RecordType == 'CopilotInteraction'\r\n| mv-expand r = LLMEventData.AccessedResources\r\n| where tobool(r.XPIADetected) == true\r\n| where '{AgentSearch}' == '' or AgentName has '{AgentSearch}' or ActorName has '{AgentSearch}'\n| project TimeGenerated, ThreatLevel = '🔴 XPIA', AgentName, ActorName, SiteUrl = tostring(r.SiteUrl), Action = tostring(r.Action), Type = tostring(r.Type)\r\n| order by TimeGenerated desc\r\n| take 100",
              "size": 0,
              "title": "XPIA — indirect injection on accessed resources",
              "gridSettings": {
                "formatters": [
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "ThreatLevel",
                    "formatter": 0
                  }
                ]
              },
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{Workspace}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "cp-xpia"
          },
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "### 🔌 Plugins / config & grounding sources\n\nConfiguration events explain who changed the agent, plugin, prompt-book, or settings surface; grounding data shows which sites influenced interactions. Review unexpected changes near a security event and unusual or newly popular resource locations. Access counts indicate references in audit records, not bytes transferred, content sensitivity, or successful exfiltration."
            },
            "name": "cp-h3"
          },
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "#### Plugin, prompt-book, and settings activity\n\nThis summarizes non-interaction audit record types by actor, with affected agents and last-seen time. Use it to find unexpected publishing, plugin or connector, prompt, or settings changes around a security or reliability event. Expand the original audit record before response because `RecordType` is a broad category and this aggregate does not show the changed property or old and new values."
            },
            "name": "cp-config-desc"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "CopilotActivity\r\n| where RecordType != 'CopilotInteraction'\r\n| summarize Events = count(), Agents = make_set(AgentName, 5), LastSeen = max(TimeGenerated) by RecordType, ActorName\r\n| order by Events desc",
              "size": 0,
              "title": "Plugin / prompt-book / settings events (non-interaction RecordTypes)",
              "gridSettings": {
                "formatters": [
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "Events",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "orange"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{Workspace}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "cp-config"
          },
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "#### Grounding-source concentration\n\nThis ranks populated `AccessedResources[].SiteUrl` values by references across interactions and shows how many agents and actors touched each site. Use it to identify unexpected domains, newly popular sources, or one location influencing many agents. `Accesses` is neither bytes read nor proof of exfiltration, and URL availability and cardinality vary by Microsoft 365 workload and audit schema."
            },
            "name": "cp-rag-desc"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "CopilotActivity\r\n| where RecordType == 'CopilotInteraction'\r\n| mv-expand r = LLMEventData.AccessedResources\r\n| extend SiteUrl = tostring(r.SiteUrl)\r\n| where isnotempty(SiteUrl)\r\n| summarize Accesses = count(), Agents = dcount(AgentName), Actors = dcount(ActorName) by SiteUrl\r\n| top 25 by Accesses desc",
              "size": 0,
              "title": "Top accessed resources / RAG grounding sites",
              "gridSettings": {
                "formatters": [
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "Accesses",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "blue"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{Workspace}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "cp-rag"
          }
        ]
      },
      "name": "group-copilot"
    },
    {
      "type": 12,
      "conditionalVisibility": {
        "parameterName": "selectedTab",
        "comparison": "isEqualTo",
        "value": "studio"
      },
      "content": {
        "version": "NotebookGroup/1.0",
        "groupType": "editable",
        "items": [
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "## 🟨 Copilot Studio — AppEvents + AppDependencies\n\n**AppEvents** carries bot turns (BotMessageReceived / BotMessageSend; UserId = pva-studio<botid>); **AppDependencies** carries connector calls (AppRoleName == 'Microsoft Copilot Studio'). Message **text** tiles need **Log sensitive properties** enabled on the agent.\n\n**How to read this tab:** compare received and sent turns for channel or bot anomalies, then inspect connector latency/failures and security markers in user input or bot output. Connector and MCP panels show capability and execution metadata; a risky tool name or external destination is a review signal, not proof of exploitation. Text detections require sensitive-property logging and can expose regulated content, so restrict workspace access and prefer environment-level `InvokeAgent`/`ExecuteTool` spans for metadata-first investigations.",
              "style": "info"
            },
            "name": "st-h"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "union isfuzzy=true\r\n(AppEvents | where Name == 'BotMessageReceived' | summarize Value = count() | extend Metric = 'User messages', Order = 1),\r\n(AppEvents | where Name == 'BotMessageSend' | summarize Value = count() | extend Metric = 'Bot responses', Order = 2),\r\n(AppEvents | where Name startswith 'BotMessage' | summarize Value = dcount(tostring(Properties['conversationId'])) | extend Metric = 'Conversations', Order = 3),\r\n(AppEvents | where Name startswith 'BotMessage' | summarize Value = dcount(UserId) | extend Metric = 'Distinct bots', Order = 4),\r\n(AppEvents | where Name startswith 'BotMessage' | summarize Value = dcount(tostring(Properties['channelId'])) | extend Metric = 'Channels', Order = 5),\r\n(AppDependencies | where AppRoleName == 'Microsoft Copilot Studio' | summarize Value = count() | extend Metric = 'Connector calls', Order = 6),\r\n(AppDependencies | where AppRoleName == 'Microsoft Copilot Studio' and Success == false | summarize Value = count() | extend Metric = 'Connector failures', Order = 7)\r\n| project Order, Metric, Value\r\n| sort by Order asc",
              "size": 3,
              "visualization": "tiles",
              "title": "Copilot Studio metrics",
              "tileSettings": {
                "leftContent": {
                  "columnMatch": "Value",
                  "formatter": 12,
                  "formatOptions": {
                    "palette": "blue"
                  }
                },
                "showBorder": true,
                "titleContent": {
                  "columnMatch": "Metric",
                  "formatter": 1
                }
              },
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{Workspace}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "st-kpi"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "AppEvents\r\n| where Name startswith 'BotMessage'\r\n| summarize Events = count() by bin(TimeGenerated, 1h), Name",
              "size": 0,
              "visualization": "timechart",
              "title": "Bot turns over time (received vs sent)",
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{Workspace}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "st-time"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "AppEvents\r\n| where Name startswith 'BotMessage'\r\n| where '{AgentSearch}' == '' or UserId has '{AgentSearch}'\r\n| summarize Messages = count(), Conversations = dcount(tostring(Properties['conversationId'])), Channels = dcount(tostring(Properties['channelId'])), LastSeen = max(TimeGenerated) by BotId = UserId\r\n| top 25 by Messages desc",
              "size": 0,
              "title": "Top bots by message volume",
              "gridSettings": {
                "formatters": [
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "Messages",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "blue"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{Workspace}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "st-bots"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "AppEvents\r\n| where Name startswith 'BotMessage'\r\n| extend Channel = tostring(Properties['channelId'])\r\n| summarize Messages = count(), Bots = dcount(UserId) by Channel\r\n| top 20 by Messages desc",
              "size": 1,
              "visualization": "piechart",
              "title": "Channel distribution",
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{Workspace}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "st-channels"
          },
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "### 🔌 Connector calls & error storms\n\nConnector dependencies are the agent's path to external systems and data. Use volume, failure percentage, and latency to identify degraded connectors, new destinations, or conversation-scoped error loops. A failure storm may be an outage, bad credentials, throttling, malformed input, or abuse; correlate `OperationId`, target, result code, bot, and deployment changes before escalating."
            },
            "name": "st-h2"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "AppDependencies\r\n| where AppRoleName == 'Microsoft Copilot Studio'\r\n| extend TargetPrefix = tolower(tostring(split(Target, '/')[0]))\r\n| summarize Calls = count(), Failures = countif(Success == false), AvgMs = round(avg(DurationMs), 0), LastSeen = max(TimeGenerated) by ConnectorName = Name, TargetPrefix\r\n| extend FailPct = round(100.0 * Failures / Calls, 1)\r\n| top 25 by Calls desc",
              "size": 0,
              "title": "Connector targets — volume, failure %, latency",
              "gridSettings": {
                "formatters": [
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "Calls",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "blue"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "FailPct",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "red"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{Workspace}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "st-conn"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "AppDependencies\r\n| where AppRoleName == 'Microsoft Copilot Studio' and Success == false\r\n| extend Conversation = tostring(Properties['conversationId'])\r\n| summarize Failures = count(), Connectors = make_set(Name, 10), LastSeen = max(TimeGenerated) by Conversation\r\n| where Failures >= 10\r\n| order by Failures desc",
              "size": 0,
              "title": "Connector error storm (>=10 failures per conversation)",
              "gridSettings": {
                "formatters": [
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "Failures",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "red"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{Workspace}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "st-err"
          },
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "### 🚨 Jailbreak / direct prompt injection & sensitive content (requires text logging)\n\nThese are content-regex hunts over logged user messages and bot responses, not service-generated Prompt Shield verdicts. Treat matches as leads, validate the complete event under restricted access, and correlate with tools or connectors that could turn unsafe text into an action. If sensitive-property logging is disabled, empty panels mean the required content was not collected, not that no attack or leakage occurred."
            },
            "name": "st-h3"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "AppEvents\r\n| where Name == 'BotMessageReceived'\r\n| extend msg = tostring(Properties['text'])\r\n| where isnotempty(msg)\r\n| where msg matches regex @'(?i)(ignore (all|previous|above)|disregard .*instruction|system prompt|developer mode|jailbreak|do anything now|reveal your (instructions|prompt))'\r\n| project TimeGenerated, ThreatLevel = '🟠 Injection marker', BotId = UserId, Channel = tostring(Properties['channelId']), Conversation = tostring(Properties['conversationId']), Snippet = substring(msg, 0, 200)\r\n| order by TimeGenerated desc\r\n| take 100",
              "size": 0,
              "title": "Prompt-injection markers in user messages",
              "gridSettings": {
                "formatters": [
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "ThreatLevel",
                    "formatter": 0
                  }
                ]
              },
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{Workspace}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "st-inj"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "AppEvents\r\n| where Name == 'BotMessageSend'\r\n| extend msg = tostring(Properties['text'])\r\n| where isnotempty(msg)\r\n| where msg matches regex @'(AKIA[0-9A-Z]{16}|-----BEGIN [A-Z ]*PRIVATE KEY-----|eyJ[A-Za-z0-9_-]{8,}\\.[A-Za-z0-9_-]{8,}\\.[A-Za-z0-9_-]{8,})'\r\n| project TimeGenerated, ThreatLevel = '🔴 Secret in response', BotId = UserId, Conversation = tostring(Properties['conversationId']), Snippet = substring(msg, 0, 200)\r\n| order by TimeGenerated desc\r\n| take 100",
              "size": 0,
              "title": "Secrets in bot responses",
              "gridSettings": {
                "formatters": [
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "ThreatLevel",
                    "formatter": 0
                  }
                ]
              },
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{Workspace}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "st-sens"
          },
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "### 🔐 MCP exploitation & remote-command risk\n\nThis section supports both Copilot Studio telemetry models: connector calls identified by `AppRoleName == 'Microsoft Copilot Studio'`, `Name`, and `Target`; and environment-level `ExecuteTool` spans identified by `gen_ai.operation.name`, `gen_ai.tool.name/type`, and shared `OperationId`. Configure the approved-target list below with exact `Target` values from your reviewed inventory. Detection is metadata-only except the optional exploit-intent panel, which reads recorded input but never displays it.",
              "style": "warning"
            },
            "name": "st-mcp-h"
          },
          {
            "type": 9,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlParameterItem/1.0",
              "parameters": [
                {
                  "id": "p-approved-mcp",
                  "version": "KqlParameterItem/1.0",
                  "name": "ApprovedMcpTargets",
                  "label": "Approved MCP targets (comma-separated exact Target values)",
                  "type": 1,
                  "isRequired": false,
                  "value": ""
                }
              ],
              "style": "formVertical",
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces"
            },
            "name": "st-mcp-params"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "let Legacy = AppDependencies\n| where AppRoleName == \"Microsoft Copilot Studio\"\n| where Name has \"MCP\" or Target has \"mcp\"\n| project TimeGenerated, OperationId, Success, ResultCode, DurationMs,\n    Agent = tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.agent.name\"]),\n    Conversation = tostring(Properties[\"conversationId\"]),\n    Tool = Name, ToolType = \"MCP - connector telemetry\", Target = tostring(Target);\nlet Modern = AppDependencies\n| where tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.operation.name\"]) == \"execute_tool\"\n| extend Tool = tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.tool.name\"]), ToolType = tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.tool.type\"])\n| where Tool has \"mcp\" or ToolType has \"mcp\"\n| project TimeGenerated, OperationId, Success, ResultCode, DurationMs,\n    Agent = tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.agent.name\"]),\n    Conversation = tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.conversation.id\"]), Tool, ToolType, Target = tostring(Target);\nunion Legacy, Modern\n| summarize Calls = count(), Failures = countif(Success == false), Agents = dcountif(Agent, isnotempty(Agent)), Conversations = dcountif(Conversation, isnotempty(Conversation)), AvgMs = round(avg(DurationMs), 0), P95Ms = round(percentile(DurationMs, 95), 0), FirstSeen = min(TimeGenerated), LastSeen = max(TimeGenerated) by Tool, ToolType, Target\n| extend FailurePct = round(100.0 * Failures / Calls, 2)\n| order by Calls desc",
              "size": 0,
              "title": "MCP server and tool inventory",
              "gridSettings": {
                "formatters": [
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "Calls",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "blue"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "FailurePct",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "red"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "P95Ms",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "yellow"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{Workspace}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "st-mcp-inventory"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "let RawAllowlist = trim(\" \", \"{ApprovedMcpTargets}\");\nlet AllowlistConfigured = isnotempty(RawAllowlist);\nlet Approved = split(tolower(replace_string(RawAllowlist, \" \", \"\")), \",\");\nAppDependencies\n| where AppRoleName == \"Microsoft Copilot Studio\"\n| where Name has \"MCP\" or Target has \"mcp\"\n| extend NormalizedTarget = tolower(tostring(Target))\n| extend Approval = case(not(AllowlistConfigured), \"CONFIGURE ALLOWLIST\", set_has_element(Approved, NormalizedTarget), \"Approved\", \"UNAPPROVED\")\n| where Approval != \"Approved\"\n| summarize Calls = count(), Conversations = dcount(tostring(Properties[\"conversationId\"])), FirstSeen = min(TimeGenerated), LastSeen = max(TimeGenerated) by Approval, Tool = Name, Target = tostring(Target)\n| order by Approval desc, Calls desc",
              "size": 0,
              "title": "MCP targets outside the approved list",
              "gridSettings": {
                "formatters": [
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "Approval",
                    "formatter": 0
                  },
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "Calls",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "red"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{Workspace}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "st-mcp-allowlist"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "let Legacy = AppDependencies\n| where AppRoleName == \"Microsoft Copilot Studio\"\n| project TimeGenerated, OperationId, Success, ResultCode, Agent = \"\", Conversation = tostring(Properties[\"conversationId\"]), Tool = Name, Target = tostring(Target);\nlet Modern = AppDependencies\n| where tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.operation.name\"]) == \"execute_tool\"\n| project TimeGenerated, OperationId, Success, ResultCode, Agent = tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.agent.name\"]), Conversation = tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.conversation.id\"]), Tool = tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.tool.name\"]), Target = tostring(Target);\nunion Legacy, Modern\n| extend Search = tolower(strcat(Tool, \" \", Target))\n| where Search matches regex @\"(run[_ -]?(shell|command|code)|execute[_ -]?(shell|command|code)|powershell|cmd.exe|terminal|reverse[_ -]?shell|metasploit|kali|ssh[_ -]?exec|remote[_ -]?code[_ -]?execution|vulnerabilities/exec)\"\n| extend Signal = case(Search has_any (\"reverse shell\", \"reverse_shell\", \"metasploit\", \"vulnerabilities/exec\", \"remote code execution\"), \"CRITICAL - exploitation capability\", \"HIGH - command execution capability\")\n| summarize Calls = count(), Failures = countif(Success == false), Traces = dcount(OperationId), FirstSeen = min(TimeGenerated), LastSeen = max(TimeGenerated) by Signal, Agent, Tool, Target\n| order by Signal asc, Calls desc",
              "size": 0,
              "title": "Command-capable or offensive MCP tool names",
              "gridSettings": {
                "formatters": [
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "Signal",
                    "formatter": 0
                  },
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "Calls",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "red"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{Workspace}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "st-mcp-command-tools"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "AppDependencies\n| where AppRoleName == \"Microsoft Copilot Studio\" or tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.operation.name\"]) == \"execute_tool\"\n| extend TargetValue = tostring(Target)\n| where TargetValue startswith \"http://\" or TargetValue startswith \"https://\"\n| extend Host = tostring(parse_url(TargetValue)[\"Host\"])\n| extend Classification = case(Host endswith \".microsoft.com\" or Host endswith \".microsoftonline.com\" or Host endswith \".azure.com\", \"Microsoft\", Host in (\"localhost\", \"127.0.0.1\"), \"Local\", \"EXTERNAL - REVIEW\")\n| summarize Calls = count(), Failures = countif(Success == false), Agents = make_set(tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.agent.name\"]), 10), FirstSeen = min(TimeGenerated), LastSeen = max(TimeGenerated) by Classification, Host, TargetValue\n| order by Classification desc, Calls desc",
              "size": 0,
              "title": "Explicit external MCP / connector URL targets",
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{Workspace}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "st-mcp-external"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "let Roots = AppDependencies\n| where tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.operation.name\"]) == \"invoke_agent\"\n| summarize Agent = take_any(tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.agent.name\"])), Conversation = take_any(tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.conversation.id\"])), User = take_any(coalesce(tostring(Properties[\"user.email\"]), tostring(Properties[\"user.id\"]))), Channel = take_any(tostring(Properties[\"microsoft.channel.name\"])), RootSuccess = take_any(Success) by OperationId;\nlet Tools = AppDependencies\n| where tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.operation.name\"]) == \"execute_tool\"\n| extend Tool = tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.tool.name\"]), ToolType = tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.tool.type\"])\n| where Tool has \"mcp\" or ToolType has \"mcp\"\n| summarize ToolCalls = count(), MCPTools = make_set(Tool, 20), ToolTypes = make_set(ToolType, 10), ToolFailures = countif(Success == false), LastToolCall = max(TimeGenerated) by OperationId;\nRoots\n| join kind=inner Tools on OperationId\n| project LastToolCall, OperationId, Agent, Conversation, User, Channel, MCPTools, ToolTypes, ToolCalls, ToolFailures, RootSuccess\n| order by LastToolCall desc\n| take 100",
              "size": 0,
              "title": "Agent → MCP execution chains (environment telemetry)",
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{Workspace}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "st-mcp-trace-chain"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "union isfuzzy=true\n(AppEvents\n| where Name == \"BotMessageReceived\"\n| project TimeGenerated, TraceId = OperationId, Agent = UserId, Conversation = tostring(Properties[\"conversationId\"]), Content = tostring(Properties[\"text\"]), Source = \"Agent-level event\"),\n(AppDependencies\n| where tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.operation.name\"]) == \"invoke_agent\"\n| project TimeGenerated, TraceId = OperationId, Agent = tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.agent.name\"]), Conversation = tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.conversation.id\"]), Content = tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.input.messages\"]), Source = \"Environment span\"),\n(AppGenAIContent\n| where isnotempty(InputMessages)\n| project TimeGenerated, TraceId, Agent = AgentName, Conversation = tostring(Attributes[\"gen_ai.conversation.id\"]), Content = InputMessages, Source = \"Protected GenAI content\")\n| where isnotempty(Content)\n| summarize arg_max(TimeGenerated, *) by TraceId, Agent, Conversation\n| where Content has_any (\"remote code execution\", \"reverse shell\", \"metasploit\", \"run_shell_command\", \"vulnerabilities/exec\", \"kali linux\", \"execute command\", \"ejecuta el comando\", \"ejecuta un comando\")\n    or Content matches regex @\"(?i)(execute|ejecuta|run).{0,40}(command|comando|shell)\"\n| extend Signal = case(Content has_any (\"reverse shell\", \"metasploit\", \"vulnerabilities/exec\", \"run_shell_command\"), \"CRITICAL - exploit/tool execution intent\", \"HIGH - remote command or RCE intent\")\n| project TimeGenerated, Signal, Agent, Conversation, TraceId, Source\n| order by TimeGenerated desc\n| take 100",
              "size": 0,
              "title": "Exploit / RCE / remote-command intent in agent input (content logging required)",
              "gridSettings": {
                "formatters": [
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "Signal",
                    "formatter": 0
                  }
                ]
              },
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{Workspace}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "st-mcp-exploit-intent"
          },
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "### Mitigation for the Copilot Studio → MCP → remote-execution scenario\n\n- Use **Advanced connector policies** as a strict allowlist and block unapproved MCP servers. Current MCP governance blocks at server level, not individual tool level.\n- Keep classic **Power Platform data policies** in mixed mode where needed to block custom connectors, HTTP requests, skills, and disallowed endpoints; MCP tools that rely on blocked Power Platform connectors are also blocked.\n- Require **Microsoft Entra authentication**, isolate dev/test/prod environments, and apply least-privilege permissions to the identity used by each connector or MCP server.\n- Do not expose a general-purpose shell, command, SSH, code-execution, or penetration-testing MCP server to production agents. If an administrative action is required, use narrow typed operations, input validation, approval, and constrained execution.\n- Enable environment-level Application Insights export to obtain `InvokeAgent` → `ExecuteTool` traces and alert on command-capable tools, allowlist drift, unusual external destinations, and exploit intent.\n- Use network egress controls on self-hosted MCP infrastructure so a compromised agent cannot reach arbitrary targets.\n\nSee `COPILOT-STUDIO-MCP-SECURITY.md` for the control checklist and limitations.",
              "style": "info"
            },
            "name": "st-mcp-notes"
          }
        ]
      },
      "name": "group-studio"
    },
    {
      "type": 12,
      "conditionalVisibility": {
        "parameterName": "selectedTab",
        "comparison": "isEqualTo",
        "value": "foundry"
      },
      "content": {
        "version": "NotebookGroup/1.0",
        "groupType": "editable",
        "items": [
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "## 🟪 Azure AI Foundry Agents — AppDependencies (gen_ai.*)\n\nReads Foundry OpenTelemetry spans in **AppDependencies** where Properties['gen_ai.*'] is present. Text-content tiles require AZURE_TRACING_GEN_AI_CONTENT_RECORDING_ENABLED=true.\n\n**How to read this tab:** use spans, conversations, tokens, and tools to identify the agent and model driving demand, then inspect guardrail verdicts and prompt-attack indicators for the same time window. A content-filter hit shows that a configured control evaluated content; it does not by itself prove compromise or blocking. Raw regex matches are heuristic and require analyst validation. From September 30, 2026, sensitive GenAI values move to protected `AppGenAIContent`; structural trace attributes remain in `AppDependencies`.",
              "style": "info"
            },
            "name": "fo-h"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "union isfuzzy=true\r\n(AppDependencies | where isnotempty(tostring(Properties['gen_ai.agent.name'])) | summarize Value = count() | extend Metric = 'Agent spans', Order = 1),\r\n(AppDependencies | where isnotempty(tostring(Properties['gen_ai.agent.name'])) | summarize Value = dcount(tostring(Properties['gen_ai.agent.name'])) | extend Metric = 'Distinct agents', Order = 2),\r\n(AppDependencies | where isnotempty(tostring(Properties['gen_ai.conversation.id'])) | summarize Value = dcount(tostring(Properties['gen_ai.conversation.id'])) | extend Metric = 'Conversations', Order = 3),\r\n(AppDependencies | where isnotempty(tostring(Properties['gen_ai.tool.name'])) | summarize Value = count() | extend Metric = 'Tool calls', Order = 4),\r\n(AppDependencies | summarize Value = sum(tolong(Properties['gen_ai.usage.input_tokens'])) | extend Metric = 'Input tokens', Order = 5),\r\n(AppDependencies | summarize Value = sum(tolong(Properties['gen_ai.usage.output_tokens'])) | extend Metric = 'Output tokens', Order = 6),\r\n(AppDependencies | where isnotempty(tostring(Properties['microsoft.foundry.content_filter.results'])) | summarize Value = count() | extend Metric = 'Content-filter hits', Order = 7)\r\n| project Order, Metric, Value\r\n| sort by Order asc",
              "size": 3,
              "visualization": "tiles",
              "title": "Foundry agent metrics",
              "tileSettings": {
                "leftContent": {
                  "columnMatch": "Value",
                  "formatter": 12,
                  "formatOptions": {
                    "palette": "blue"
                  }
                },
                "showBorder": true,
                "titleContent": {
                  "columnMatch": "Metric",
                  "formatter": 1
                }
              },
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{Workspace}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "fo-kpi"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "AppDependencies\r\n| where isnotempty(tostring(Properties['gen_ai.agent.name']))\r\n| summarize Spans = count() by bin(TimeGenerated, 1h)",
              "size": 0,
              "visualization": "timechart",
              "title": "Agent spans over time",
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{Workspace}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "fo-time"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "AppDependencies\r\n| where isnotempty(tostring(Properties['gen_ai.agent.name']))\r\n| extend Agent = tostring(Properties['gen_ai.agent.name']), Model = tostring(Properties['gen_ai.request.model'])\r\n| where '{AgentSearch}' == '' or Agent has '{AgentSearch}' or Model has '{AgentSearch}'\r\n| summarize Spans = count(), Conversations = dcount(tostring(Properties['gen_ai.conversation.id'])), InputTokens = sum(tolong(Properties['gen_ai.usage.input_tokens'])), OutputTokens = sum(tolong(Properties['gen_ai.usage.output_tokens'])), LastSeen = max(TimeGenerated) by Agent\r\n| top 25 by Spans desc",
              "size": 0,
              "title": "Top agents — spans, conversations, tokens",
              "gridSettings": {
                "formatters": [
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "Spans",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "blue"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "InputTokens",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "purple"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "OutputTokens",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "purple"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{Workspace}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "fo-agents"
          },
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "### 🛠️ Tool usage & token cost\n\nTool calls define what an agent can do; token trends show the consumption associated with model activity. Investigate a new or dominant tool, sharp token growth, repeated calls within one conversation, and failures that suggest a loop. High usage can be legitimate batch work, so compare with agent, model, release, and caller baselines before labeling denial-of-wallet abuse."
            },
            "name": "fo-h2"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "AppDependencies\r\n| where isnotempty(tostring(Properties['gen_ai.tool.name']))\r\n| extend Tool = tostring(Properties['gen_ai.tool.name']), ToolType = tostring(Properties['gen_ai.tool.type']), Agent = tostring(Properties['gen_ai.agent.name'])\r\n| summarize Calls = count(), Agents = dcount(Agent), Conversations = dcount(tostring(Properties['gen_ai.conversation.id'])) by Tool, ToolType\r\n| top 25 by Calls desc",
              "size": 0,
              "title": "Tool usage (gen_ai.tool.name / type)",
              "gridSettings": {
                "formatters": [
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "Calls",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "blue"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{Workspace}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "fo-tools"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "AppDependencies\r\n| where isnotempty(tostring(Properties['gen_ai.agent.name']))\r\n| extend Model = tostring(Properties['gen_ai.request.model'])\r\n| summarize InputTokens = sum(tolong(Properties['gen_ai.usage.input_tokens'])), OutputTokens = sum(tolong(Properties['gen_ai.usage.output_tokens'])) by bin(TimeGenerated, 1h), Model",
              "size": 0,
              "visualization": "barchart",
              "title": "Token usage over time by model (denial-of-wallet)",
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{Workspace}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "fo-tokens"
          },
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "### 🔐 MCP exploitation & remote-command risk\n\nFoundry agents can reach MCP servers directly or through a Foundry toolbox. These panels use `AppDependencies` tool spans and W3C `OperationId`; MCP classification checks `gen_ai.tool.name/type`, operation, server label/URL variants, description, and dependency target because preview SDKs do not emit one universal server field. The section separates **exposed capability**, **suspicious intent**, and **observed execution**. A command-capable name or external server is a review signal, not proof of exploitation. Tool arguments, results, and prompt content remain in protected `AppGenAIContent` and are never displayed here.",
              "style": "warning"
            },
            "name": "fo-mcp-h"
          },
          {
            "type": 9,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlParameterItem/1.0",
              "parameters": [
                {
                  "id": "p-foundry-approved-mcp",
                  "version": "KqlParameterItem/1.0",
                  "name": "ApprovedFoundryMcpTargets",
                  "label": "Approved Foundry MCP servers (comma-separated exact URL, label, or Target)",
                  "type": 1,
                  "isRequired": false,
                  "value": ""
                }
              ],
              "style": "formVertical",
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces"
            },
            "name": "fo-mcp-params"
          },
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "#### MCP server and tool inventory\n\nThis is observed execution inventory, grouped by emitted server, tool, type, agent, and model. Review first/last seen, failure rate, and conversation breadth to establish normal use. `(server metadata not emitted)` means the span identifies an MCP tool but does not expose a stable server URL or label; improve instrumentation before relying on server-level allowlisting."
            },
            "name": "fo-mcp-inventory-desc"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "AppDependencies\n| where isnotempty(tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.tool.name\"]))\n| extend Agent = tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.agent.name\"]),\n    Conversation = tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.conversation.id\"]),\n    Model = tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.request.model\"]),\n    Tool = tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.tool.name\"]),\n    ToolType = tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.tool.type\"]),\n    ToolDescription = tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.tool.description\"]),\n    ServerLabel = coalesce(tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.tool.server_label\"]), tostring(Properties[\"mcp.server.label\"]), tostring(Properties[\"server_label\"])),\n    ServerUrl = coalesce(tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.tool.server_url\"]), tostring(Properties[\"mcp.server.url\"]), tostring(Properties[\"server_url\"])),\n    Operation = tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.operation.name\"])\n| extend McpServer = coalesce(ServerUrl, ServerLabel, tostring(Target))\n| where ToolType has \"mcp\" or Operation has \"mcp\" or Tool has \"mcp\" or ToolDescription has \"mcp\" or McpServer has \"mcp\"\n| extend McpServer = iff(isempty(McpServer), \"(server metadata not emitted)\", McpServer)\n| project TimeGenerated, OperationId, Id, Success, ResultCode, DurationMs, Agent, Conversation, Model, Tool, ToolType, ToolDescription, McpServer, ServerLabel, ServerUrl, Target\n| where \"{AgentSearch}\" == \"\" or Agent has \"{AgentSearch}\" or Tool has \"{AgentSearch}\" or McpServer has \"{AgentSearch}\"\n| summarize Calls = count(), Failures = countif(Success == false), Conversations = dcountif(Conversation, isnotempty(Conversation)), AvgMs = round(avg(DurationMs), 0), P95Ms = round(percentile(DurationMs, 95), 0), FirstSeen = min(TimeGenerated), LastSeen = max(TimeGenerated) by McpServer, Tool, ToolType, Agent, Model\n| extend FailurePct = round(100.0 * Failures / Calls, 2)\n| order by Calls desc",
              "size": 0,
              "title": "Foundry MCP server and tool inventory",
              "gridSettings": {
                "formatters": [
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "Calls",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "blue"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "FailurePct",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "red"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "P95Ms",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "yellow"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{Workspace}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "fo-mcp-inventory"
          },
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "#### Server allowlist drift\n\nConfigure the exact server URL, label, or dependency `Target` values approved for this environment. Unlisted observed servers require ownership, connection, authentication, data-handling, and tool-scope review. An unconfigured allowlist is reported explicitly; missing server metadata is kept separate because it cannot be evaluated safely."
            },
            "name": "fo-mcp-allowlist-desc"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "let RawAllowlist = trim(\" \", \"{ApprovedFoundryMcpTargets}\");\nlet AllowlistConfigured = isnotempty(RawAllowlist);\nlet Approved = split(tolower(replace_string(RawAllowlist, \" \", \"\")), \",\");\nAppDependencies\n| where isnotempty(tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.tool.name\"]))\n| extend Agent = tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.agent.name\"]),\n    Conversation = tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.conversation.id\"]),\n    Model = tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.request.model\"]),\n    Tool = tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.tool.name\"]),\n    ToolType = tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.tool.type\"]),\n    ToolDescription = tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.tool.description\"]),\n    ServerLabel = coalesce(tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.tool.server_label\"]), tostring(Properties[\"mcp.server.label\"]), tostring(Properties[\"server_label\"])),\n    ServerUrl = coalesce(tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.tool.server_url\"]), tostring(Properties[\"mcp.server.url\"]), tostring(Properties[\"server_url\"])),\n    Operation = tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.operation.name\"])\n| extend McpServer = coalesce(ServerUrl, ServerLabel, tostring(Target))\n| where ToolType has \"mcp\" or Operation has \"mcp\" or Tool has \"mcp\" or ToolDescription has \"mcp\" or McpServer has \"mcp\"\n| extend McpServer = iff(isempty(McpServer), \"(server metadata not emitted)\", McpServer)\n| project TimeGenerated, OperationId, Id, Success, ResultCode, DurationMs, Agent, Conversation, Model, Tool, ToolType, ToolDescription, McpServer, ServerLabel, ServerUrl, Target\n| extend NormalizedServer = tolower(McpServer)\n| extend Approval = case(McpServer == \"(server metadata not emitted)\", \"NO SERVER METADATA\", not(AllowlistConfigured), \"CONFIGURE ALLOWLIST\", set_has_element(Approved, NormalizedServer), \"Approved\", \"UNAPPROVED\")\n| where Approval != \"Approved\"\n| where \"{AgentSearch}\" == \"\" or Agent has \"{AgentSearch}\" or Tool has \"{AgentSearch}\" or McpServer has \"{AgentSearch}\"\n| summarize Calls = count(), Agents = dcountif(Agent, isnotempty(Agent)), Conversations = dcountif(Conversation, isnotempty(Conversation)), FirstSeen = min(TimeGenerated), LastSeen = max(TimeGenerated) by Approval, McpServer, Tool\n| order by Approval desc, Calls desc",
              "size": 0,
              "title": "Foundry MCP servers outside the approved list",
              "gridSettings": {
                "formatters": [
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "Approval",
                    "formatter": 0
                  },
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "Calls",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "red"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{Workspace}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "fo-mcp-allowlist"
          },
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "#### Command-capable MCP tools\n\nNames and descriptions associated with shell, command, code execution, SSH, offensive tooling, or RCE-like operations are high-risk capabilities. Confirm whether each operation is necessary, narrowly typed, schema-validated, least privileged, and approval-gated. Name matching can miss disguised capabilities or flag benign administration tools, so validate the server's reviewed tool definition."
            },
            "name": "fo-mcp-command-tools-desc"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "AppDependencies\n| where isnotempty(tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.tool.name\"]))\n| extend Agent = tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.agent.name\"]),\n    Conversation = tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.conversation.id\"]),\n    Model = tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.request.model\"]),\n    Tool = tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.tool.name\"]),\n    ToolType = tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.tool.type\"]),\n    ToolDescription = tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.tool.description\"]),\n    ServerLabel = coalesce(tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.tool.server_label\"]), tostring(Properties[\"mcp.server.label\"]), tostring(Properties[\"server_label\"])),\n    ServerUrl = coalesce(tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.tool.server_url\"]), tostring(Properties[\"mcp.server.url\"]), tostring(Properties[\"server_url\"])),\n    Operation = tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.operation.name\"])\n| extend McpServer = coalesce(ServerUrl, ServerLabel, tostring(Target))\n| where ToolType has \"mcp\" or Operation has \"mcp\" or Tool has \"mcp\" or ToolDescription has \"mcp\" or McpServer has \"mcp\"\n| extend McpServer = iff(isempty(McpServer), \"(server metadata not emitted)\", McpServer)\n| project TimeGenerated, OperationId, Id, Success, ResultCode, DurationMs, Agent, Conversation, Model, Tool, ToolType, ToolDescription, McpServer, ServerLabel, ServerUrl, Target\n| extend Search = tolower(strcat(Tool, \" \", ToolDescription, \" \", McpServer))\n| where Search matches regex @\"(run[_ -]?(shell|command|code)|execute[_ -]?(shell|command|code)|powershell|cmd\\.exe|terminal|reverse[_ -]?shell|metasploit|kali|ssh[_ -]?exec|remote[_ -]?code[_ -]?execution|vulnerabilities/exec)\"\n| extend Signal = case(Search has_any (\"reverse shell\", \"reverse_shell\", \"metasploit\", \"vulnerabilities/exec\", \"remote code execution\"), \"CRITICAL - exploitation capability\", \"HIGH - command execution capability\")\n| where \"{AgentSearch}\" == \"\" or Agent has \"{AgentSearch}\" or Tool has \"{AgentSearch}\" or McpServer has \"{AgentSearch}\"\n| summarize Calls = count(), Failures = countif(Success == false), Traces = dcount(OperationId), Conversations = dcountif(Conversation, isnotempty(Conversation)), FirstSeen = min(TimeGenerated), LastSeen = max(TimeGenerated) by Signal, Agent, Tool, McpServer\n| order by Signal asc, Calls desc",
              "size": 0,
              "title": "Command-capable or offensive Foundry MCP tools",
              "gridSettings": {
                "formatters": [
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "Signal",
                    "formatter": 0
                  },
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "Calls",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "red"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{Workspace}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "fo-mcp-command-tools"
          },
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "#### External MCP destinations\n\nThis panel evaluates only explicit HTTP/S server metadata. Microsoft-hosted and loopback destinations are separated from other external hosts; `EXTERNAL - REVIEW` means review is required, not that the endpoint is malicious. Verify TLS, ownership, data residency, authentication, project connection, egress policy, and whether traffic should route through APIM AI Gateway."
            },
            "name": "fo-mcp-external-desc"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "AppDependencies\n| where isnotempty(tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.tool.name\"]))\n| extend Agent = tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.agent.name\"]),\n    Conversation = tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.conversation.id\"]),\n    Model = tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.request.model\"]),\n    Tool = tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.tool.name\"]),\n    ToolType = tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.tool.type\"]),\n    ToolDescription = tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.tool.description\"]),\n    ServerLabel = coalesce(tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.tool.server_label\"]), tostring(Properties[\"mcp.server.label\"]), tostring(Properties[\"server_label\"])),\n    ServerUrl = coalesce(tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.tool.server_url\"]), tostring(Properties[\"mcp.server.url\"]), tostring(Properties[\"server_url\"])),\n    Operation = tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.operation.name\"])\n| extend McpServer = coalesce(ServerUrl, ServerLabel, tostring(Target))\n| where ToolType has \"mcp\" or Operation has \"mcp\" or Tool has \"mcp\" or ToolDescription has \"mcp\" or McpServer has \"mcp\"\n| extend McpServer = iff(isempty(McpServer), \"(server metadata not emitted)\", McpServer)\n| project TimeGenerated, OperationId, Id, Success, ResultCode, DurationMs, Agent, Conversation, Model, Tool, ToolType, ToolDescription, McpServer, ServerLabel, ServerUrl, Target\n| where McpServer startswith \"http://\" or McpServer startswith \"https://\"\n| extend Host = tostring(parse_url(McpServer)[\"Host\"])\n| extend Classification = case(Host endswith \".microsoft.com\" or Host endswith \".microsoftonline.com\" or Host endswith \".azure.com\" or Host endswith \".azure.net\", \"Microsoft / Azure\", Host in (\"localhost\", \"127.0.0.1\", \"::1\"), \"Local\", \"EXTERNAL - REVIEW\")\n| where \"{AgentSearch}\" == \"\" or Agent has \"{AgentSearch}\" or Tool has \"{AgentSearch}\" or Host has \"{AgentSearch}\"\n| summarize Calls = count(), Failures = countif(Success == false), Agents = make_set_if(Agent, isnotempty(Agent), 10), Tools = make_set(Tool, 20), FirstSeen = min(TimeGenerated), LastSeen = max(TimeGenerated) by Classification, Host, McpServer\n| order by Classification desc, Calls desc",
              "size": 0,
              "title": "Explicit external Foundry MCP server targets",
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{Workspace}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "fo-mcp-external"
          },
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "#### Agent-to-MCP execution chains\n\nThis joins MCP tool spans to other Foundry spans sharing the same W3C `OperationId`, producing one trace-level row with agent, model, conversation, tools, failures, and duration. Use the operation ID in Application Insights transaction search to reconstruct parent/child ordering. Shared IDs establish trace correlation, not proof that every listed model span caused every tool call."
            },
            "name": "fo-mcp-trace-chain-desc"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "let Roots = AppDependencies\n| where isnotempty(tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.agent.name\"]))\n| summarize Agent = take_any(tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.agent.name\"])), Model = take_any(tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.request.model\"])), Conversation = take_any(tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.conversation.id\"])), RootFailures = countif(Success == false), RootSpans = count() by OperationId;\nlet MCPTools = AppDependencies\n| where isnotempty(tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.tool.name\"]))\n| extend Agent = tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.agent.name\"]),\n    Conversation = tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.conversation.id\"]),\n    Model = tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.request.model\"]),\n    Tool = tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.tool.name\"]),\n    ToolType = tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.tool.type\"]),\n    ToolDescription = tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.tool.description\"]),\n    ServerLabel = coalesce(tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.tool.server_label\"]), tostring(Properties[\"mcp.server.label\"]), tostring(Properties[\"server_label\"])),\n    ServerUrl = coalesce(tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.tool.server_url\"]), tostring(Properties[\"mcp.server.url\"]), tostring(Properties[\"server_url\"])),\n    Operation = tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.operation.name\"])\n| extend McpServer = coalesce(ServerUrl, ServerLabel, tostring(Target))\n| where ToolType has \"mcp\" or Operation has \"mcp\" or Tool has \"mcp\" or ToolDescription has \"mcp\" or McpServer has \"mcp\"\n| extend McpServer = iff(isempty(McpServer), \"(server metadata not emitted)\", McpServer)\n| project TimeGenerated, OperationId, Id, Success, ResultCode, DurationMs, Agent, Conversation, Model, Tool, ToolType, ToolDescription, McpServer, ServerLabel, ServerUrl, Target\n| summarize ToolCalls = count(), MCPTools = make_set(Tool, 20), MCPServers = make_set(McpServer, 10), ToolFailures = countif(Success == false), ToolDurationMs = round(sum(DurationMs), 0), LastToolCall = max(TimeGenerated) by OperationId;\nRoots\n| join kind=inner MCPTools on OperationId\n| where \"{AgentSearch}\" == \"\" or Agent has \"{AgentSearch}\" or tostring(MCPTools) has \"{AgentSearch}\" or tostring(MCPServers) has \"{AgentSearch}\"\n| project LastToolCall, OperationId, Agent, Model, Conversation, MCPServers, MCPTools, ToolCalls, ToolFailures, ToolDurationMs, RootSpans, RootFailures\n| order by LastToolCall desc\n| take 100",
              "size": 0,
              "title": "Foundry agent → MCP execution chains",
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{Workspace}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "fo-mcp-trace-chain"
          },
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "#### Exploit intent correlated with command execution\n\nThis higher-confidence hunt requires both a remote-command or exploitation marker in recorded agent input and a command-capable MCP tool in the same trace. It reads legacy content and protected `AppGenAIContent`, deduplicates dual-routed records, and returns metadata only. A match still requires review of user intent, approval evidence, arguments/results under privileged access, target impact, and whether the tool succeeded."
            },
            "name": "fo-mcp-exploit-chain-desc"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "let Inputs = union isfuzzy=true\n(AppDependencies\n| where isnotempty(tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.agent.name\"]))\n| extend ContentKey = strcat(OperationId, \":\", Id), TraceId = OperationId, InputAgent = tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.agent.name\"]), InputConversation = tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.conversation.id\"]), Content = tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.input.messages\"]), Source = \"Legacy dependency content\"),\n(AppGenAIContent\n| extend ContentKey = strcat(TraceId, \":\", SpanId), InputAgent = tostring(AgentName), InputConversation = tostring(Attributes[\"gen_ai.conversation.id\"]), Content = tostring(InputMessages), Source = \"Protected GenAI content\")\n| where isnotempty(Content)\n| summarize arg_max(TimeGenerated, *) by ContentKey\n| where Content has_any (\"remote code execution\", \"reverse shell\", \"metasploit\", \"run_shell_command\", \"vulnerabilities/exec\", \"kali linux\", \"execute command\")\n    or Content matches regex @\"(?i)(execute|run).{0,40}(command|shell|powershell|terminal)\"\n| summarize IntentTime = max(TimeGenerated), InputSources = make_set(Source, 3), InputAgent = take_any(InputAgent), InputConversation = take_any(InputConversation) by TraceId;\nlet CommandTools = AppDependencies\n| where isnotempty(tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.tool.name\"]))\n| extend Agent = tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.agent.name\"]),\n    Conversation = tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.conversation.id\"]),\n    Model = tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.request.model\"]),\n    Tool = tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.tool.name\"]),\n    ToolType = tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.tool.type\"]),\n    ToolDescription = tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.tool.description\"]),\n    ServerLabel = coalesce(tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.tool.server_label\"]), tostring(Properties[\"mcp.server.label\"]), tostring(Properties[\"server_label\"])),\n    ServerUrl = coalesce(tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.tool.server_url\"]), tostring(Properties[\"mcp.server.url\"]), tostring(Properties[\"server_url\"])),\n    Operation = tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.operation.name\"])\n| extend McpServer = coalesce(ServerUrl, ServerLabel, tostring(Target))\n| where ToolType has \"mcp\" or Operation has \"mcp\" or Tool has \"mcp\" or ToolDescription has \"mcp\" or McpServer has \"mcp\"\n| extend McpServer = iff(isempty(McpServer), \"(server metadata not emitted)\", McpServer)\n| project TimeGenerated, OperationId, Id, Success, ResultCode, DurationMs, Agent, Conversation, Model, Tool, ToolType, ToolDescription, McpServer, ServerLabel, ServerUrl, Target\n| extend Search = tolower(strcat(Tool, \" \", ToolDescription, \" \", McpServer))\n| where Search matches regex @\"(run[_ -]?(shell|command|code)|execute[_ -]?(shell|command|code)|powershell|cmd\\.exe|terminal|reverse[_ -]?shell|metasploit|kali|ssh[_ -]?exec|remote[_ -]?code[_ -]?execution|vulnerabilities/exec)\"\n| summarize ToolTime = max(TimeGenerated), Tools = make_set(Tool, 20), MCPServers = make_set(McpServer, 10), ToolCalls = count(), ToolFailures = countif(Success == false), ToolAgent = take_any(Agent), ToolConversation = take_any(Conversation) by OperationId;\nInputs\n| join kind=inner CommandTools on $left.TraceId == $right.OperationId\n| extend Agent = coalesce(InputAgent, ToolAgent), Conversation = coalesce(InputConversation, ToolConversation), Signal = iff(ToolFailures < ToolCalls, \"CRITICAL - intent with successful command-capable call\", \"HIGH - intent with failed command-capable call\")\n| where \"{AgentSearch}\" == \"\" or Agent has \"{AgentSearch}\" or tostring(Tools) has \"{AgentSearch}\" or tostring(MCPServers) has \"{AgentSearch}\"\n| project ToolTime, IntentTime, Signal, Agent, Conversation, TraceId, MCPServers, Tools, ToolCalls, ToolFailures, InputSources\n| order by ToolTime desc\n| take 100",
              "size": 0,
              "title": "Exploit / remote-command intent followed by Foundry MCP execution",
              "gridSettings": {
                "formatters": [
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "Signal",
                    "formatter": 0
                  }
                ]
              },
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{Workspace}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "fo-mcp-exploit-chain"
          },
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "### Mitigation for Foundry agent → MCP execution\n\n- Configure `allowed_tools`; omitting it can expose every tool returned by the server.\n- Require approval for consequential operations and enforce it in the agent runtime. A system-prompt instruction is not an approval control, and toolbox MCP endpoints do not block `tools/call` by themselves.\n- Treat tool descriptions, annotations, arguments, results, and other server output as untrusted input; validate structured schemas and authorize each operation server-side.\n- Use an agent identity or managed identity with least-privilege project connections and downstream permissions. Separate development, test, and production identities and servers.\n- Do not expose general-purpose shell, command, SSH, code-execution, or penetration-testing MCP tools to production agents. Replace them with narrow typed operations and constrained execution.\n- Route MCP traffic through APIM AI Gateway when centralized authentication, IP filtering, quotas, token/request limits, and destination monitoring are required.\n- Keep content recording disabled in production unless approved. Protect `AppGenAIContent` and require privileged monitoring access for arguments, results, prompts, and responses.",
              "style": "info"
            },
            "name": "fo-mcp-notes"
          },
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "### 🚨 Guardrail verdicts & prompt injection\n\nContent-filter and Prompt Shield metadata are control verdicts; the prompt-injection panel is a lower-confidence regex hunt over recorded input. Distinguish direct user-prompt attacks from indirect attacks in grounding content and from harm-category or custom-blocklist matches. Verify whether the policy audited or blocked the request and whether any downstream action occurred. Sensitive content belongs in protected `AppGenAIContent` with restricted access."
            },
            "name": "fo-h3"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "AppDependencies\r\n| where isnotempty(tostring(Properties['microsoft.foundry.content_filter.results']))\r\n| extend cf = tostring(Properties['microsoft.foundry.content_filter.results'])\r\n| extend Jailbreak = cf has 'jailbreak', PromptShield = cf has 'prompt_shield', Indirect = cf has 'indirect_attack', Blocklist = cf has 'custom_blocklists'\r\n| extend Verdict = case(Jailbreak, '🔴 Jailbreak', Indirect, '🟠 Indirect injection', PromptShield, '🟠 Prompt shield', Blocklist, '🟡 Blocklist', '🟡 Content-safety')\r\n| project TimeGenerated, Verdict, Agent = tostring(Properties['gen_ai.agent.name']), Conversation = tostring(Properties['gen_ai.conversation.id'])\r\n| order by TimeGenerated desc\r\n| take 100",
              "size": 0,
              "title": "Content-filter / Prompt Shield verdicts",
              "gridSettings": {
                "formatters": [
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "Verdict",
                    "formatter": 0
                  }
                ]
              },
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{Workspace}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "fo-guard"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "let RecordedInputs = union isfuzzy=true\n(AppDependencies\n| where isnotempty(tostring(Properties['gen_ai.agent.name']))\n| extend ContentKey = strcat(OperationId, \":\", Id), Trace = OperationId,\n    Agent = tostring(Properties['gen_ai.agent.name']),\n    Conversation = tostring(Properties['gen_ai.conversation.id']),\n    RecordedInput = tostring(Properties['gen_ai.input.messages'])),\n(AppGenAIContent\n| extend ContentKey = strcat(TraceId, \":\", SpanId), Trace = TraceId,\n    Agent = tostring(AgentName),\n    Conversation = tostring(Attributes['gen_ai.conversation.id']),\n    RecordedInput = tostring(InputMessages))\n| where isnotempty(RecordedInput)\n| summarize arg_max(TimeGenerated, *) by ContentKey;\nRecordedInputs\n| where RecordedInput matches regex @'(?i)(ignore (all|previous|above)|disregard .*instruction|system prompt|jailbreak|do anything now)'\n| project TimeGenerated, ThreatLevel = '🟠 Heuristic injection marker', Agent, Conversation, Trace\n| order by TimeGenerated desc\n| take 100",
              "size": 0,
              "title": "Prompt-injection markers in agent input",
              "gridSettings": {
                "formatters": [
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "ThreatLevel",
                    "formatter": 0
                  }
                ]
              },
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{Workspace}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "fo-inj"
          }
        ]
      },
      "name": "group-foundry"
    },
    {
      "type": 12,
      "conditionalVisibility": {
        "parameterName": "selectedTab",
        "comparison": "isEqualTo",
        "value": "openai"
      },
      "content": {
        "version": "NotebookGroup/1.0",
        "groupType": "editable",
        "items": [
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "## 🟩 OpenAI Connector — ASimAgentEventLogs + OpenAIAuditLogs\n\nRuntime completions in **ASimAgentEventLogs** / OpenAIChatCompletions (ModelName, tokens, ToolName, AdditionalFields.input_user); org audit in **OpenAIAuditLogs**.\n\n**How to read this tab:** use completion and token trends for adoption and cost, `input_user` for caller attribution, tool names for capability drift, and organization audit events for administrative changes. Empty users mean the caller did not populate the optional attribution field; do not treat them as anonymous authentication. Token totals depend on connector parsing and provider responses, while audit-event names vary by connector schema and should be expanded before alerting.",
              "style": "info"
            },
            "name": "oa-h"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "union isfuzzy=true\r\n(ASimAgentEventLogs | summarize Value = count() | extend Metric = 'Completions / events', Order = 1),\r\n(ASimAgentEventLogs | summarize Value = dcount(ModelName) | extend Metric = 'Distinct models', Order = 2),\r\n(ASimAgentEventLogs | summarize Value = sum(tolong(InputTokensUsed)) | extend Metric = 'Input tokens', Order = 3),\r\n(ASimAgentEventLogs | summarize Value = sum(tolong(OutputTokensUsed)) | extend Metric = 'Output tokens', Order = 4),\r\n(ASimAgentEventLogs | where isnotempty(ToolName) | summarize Value = count() | extend Metric = 'Tool calls', Order = 5),\r\n(OpenAIAuditLogs | summarize Value = count() | extend Metric = 'Audit events', Order = 6)\r\n| project Order, Metric, Value\r\n| sort by Order asc",
              "size": 3,
              "visualization": "tiles",
              "title": "OpenAI metrics",
              "tileSettings": {
                "leftContent": {
                  "columnMatch": "Value",
                  "formatter": 12,
                  "formatOptions": {
                    "palette": "blue"
                  }
                },
                "showBorder": true,
                "titleContent": {
                  "columnMatch": "Metric",
                  "formatter": 1
                }
              },
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{Workspace}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "oa-kpi"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "ASimAgentEventLogs\r\n| summarize Events = count() by bin(TimeGenerated, 1h), ModelName",
              "size": 0,
              "visualization": "timechart",
              "title": "Completions over time by model",
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{Workspace}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "oa-time"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "ASimAgentEventLogs\r\n| extend User = tostring(todynamic(AdditionalFields).input_user)\r\n| where '{AgentSearch}' == '' or User has '{AgentSearch}' or ModelName has '{AgentSearch}'\r\n| summarize Requests = count(), InputTokens = sum(tolong(InputTokensUsed)), OutputTokens = sum(tolong(OutputTokensUsed)), Models = make_set(ModelName, 5), LastSeen = max(TimeGenerated) by User\r\n| top 25 by Requests desc",
              "size": 0,
              "title": "Top callers (input_user) — requests & tokens",
              "gridSettings": {
                "formatters": [
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "Requests",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "blue"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "InputTokens",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "purple"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{Workspace}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "oa-users"
          },
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "### 🛠️ Tools, token cost & org audit\n\nTool names reveal capabilities used through the connector, token volume supports cost and anomaly review, and organization audit events explain administrative change. Look for first-seen or unexpectedly frequent tools, token spikes by model or caller, and key, role, quota, or settings changes near an incident. Provider event names and fields vary, so inspect a sample `OpenAIAuditLogs` record before creating a strict detection."
            },
            "name": "oa-h2"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "ASimAgentEventLogs\r\n| where isnotempty(ToolName)\r\n| summarize Calls = count(), Users = dcount(tostring(todynamic(AdditionalFields).input_user)), LastSeen = max(TimeGenerated) by ToolName\r\n| top 25 by Calls desc",
              "size": 0,
              "title": "Tool usage (ToolName)",
              "gridSettings": {
                "formatters": [
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "Calls",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "blue"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{Workspace}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "oa-tools"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "ASimAgentEventLogs\r\n| summarize InputTokens = sum(tolong(InputTokensUsed)), OutputTokens = sum(tolong(OutputTokensUsed)) by bin(TimeGenerated, 1h), ModelName",
              "size": 0,
              "visualization": "barchart",
              "title": "Token usage over time by model",
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{Workspace}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "oa-tokens"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "OpenAIAuditLogs\r\n| extend EventKind = tostring(column_ifexists('EventType', column_ifexists('OperationName', column_ifexists('Type', '(event)'))))\r\n| summarize Events = count(), LastSeen = max(TimeGenerated) by EventKind\r\n| order by Events desc",
              "size": 0,
              "title": "Org audit events (OpenAIAuditLogs)",
              "gridSettings": {
                "formatters": [
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "Events",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "orange"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{Workspace}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "oa-audit"
          }
        ]
      },
      "name": "group-openai"
    },
    {
      "type": 12,
      "conditionalVisibility": {
        "parameterName": "selectedTab",
        "comparison": "isEqualTo",
        "value": "apim"
      },
      "content": {
        "version": "NotebookGroup/1.0",
        "groupType": "editable",
        "items": [
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "## 🌐 APIM AI Gateway — API traffic + agent correlation\n\nChoose an **APIM subscription**, then set **APIM telemetry source**. Use **Application Insights** when the linked or managed Log Analytics workspace is unavailable; choose the component in **APIM Application Insights**. Use **Log Analytics workspace** when you can select the backing workspace directly.\n\nApplication Insights mode queries `requests`, `dependencies`, `exceptions`, `traces`, `customMetrics`, and `genAIContent`, with APIM metadata in `customDimensions`. Workspace mode queries the equivalent `AppRequests`, `AppDependencies`, `AppExceptions`, `AppTraces`, `AppMetrics`, and `AppGenAIContent`, with metadata in `Properties`. The panels and visualizations are paired and switch automatically with the source selector.\n\nThe AppRequests payload-security subsection intentionally displays captured input, instructions, tools, request bodies, and response bodies. This can contain credentials, personal data, regulated content, system instructions, and tool schemas. Restrict access, retention, export, screenshots, and incident copies.",
              "style": "info"
            },
            "name": "apim-h"
          },
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "#### Gateway health at a glance\n\nThese KPIs summarize APIM frontend traffic, failed requests, success rate, p95 gateway latency, backend calls/failures, and known consumers for the selected period. Use them to establish whether the issue is at the gateway, backend, or caller layer. Counts and distinct consumers are affected by Application Insights sampling and identity population; a blank consumer identity doesn't mean there was no caller."
            },
            "name": "apim-kpi-desc"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "union isfuzzy=true\n(AppRequests\n| where SDKVersion startswith \"apim:\"\n| summarize Value = todouble(count())\n| extend Metric = \"Gateway requests\", Order = 1),\n(AppRequests\n| where SDKVersion startswith \"apim:\"\n| summarize Value = todouble(countif(Success == false))\n| extend Metric = \"Failed requests\", Order = 2),\n(AppRequests\n| where SDKVersion startswith \"apim:\"\n| summarize Total = count(), Succeeded = countif(Success == true)\n| extend Value = iff(Total == 0, 0.0, round(100.0 * Succeeded / Total, 2))\n| extend Metric = \"Success %\", Order = 3),\n(AppRequests\n| where SDKVersion startswith \"apim:\"\n| summarize Value = round(percentile(DurationMs, 95), 0)\n| extend Metric = \"P95 latency ms\", Order = 4),\n(AppDependencies\n| where SDKVersion startswith \"apim:\"\n| summarize Value = todouble(count())\n| extend Metric = \"Backend calls\", Order = 5),\n(AppDependencies\n| where SDKVersion startswith \"apim:\" and Success == false\n| summarize Value = todouble(count())\n| extend Metric = \"Backend failures\", Order = 6),\n(AppRequests\n| where SDKVersion startswith \"apim:\"\n| summarize Value = todouble(dcount(coalesce(UserAuthenticatedId, UserId)))\n| extend Metric = \"Known consumers\", Order = 7)\n| project Order, Metric, Value\n| sort by Order asc",
              "size": 3,
              "visualization": "tiles",
              "title": "APIM AI Gateway metrics",
              "tileSettings": {
                "leftContent": {
                  "columnMatch": "Value",
                  "formatter": 12,
                  "formatOptions": {
                    "palette": "blue"
                  }
                },
                "showBorder": true,
                "titleContent": {
                  "columnMatch": "Metric",
                  "formatter": 1
                }
              },
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{APIMWorkspace}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "apim-kpi",
            "conditionalVisibility": {
              "parameterName": "APIMTelemetrySource",
              "comparison": "isEqualTo",
              "value": "workspace"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "union isfuzzy=true\n(requests\n| where sdkVersion startswith \"apim:\"\n| summarize Value = todouble(count())\n| extend Metric = \"Gateway requests\", Order = 1),\n(requests\n| where sdkVersion startswith \"apim:\"\n| summarize Value = todouble(countif(success == false))\n| extend Metric = \"Failed requests\", Order = 2),\n(requests\n| where sdkVersion startswith \"apim:\"\n| summarize Total = count(), Succeeded = countif(success == true)\n| extend Value = iff(Total == 0, 0.0, round(100.0 * Succeeded / Total, 2))\n| extend Metric = \"Success %\", Order = 3),\n(requests\n| where sdkVersion startswith \"apim:\"\n| summarize Value = round(percentile(duration, 95), 0)\n| extend Metric = \"P95 latency ms\", Order = 4),\n(dependencies\n| where sdkVersion startswith \"apim:\"\n| summarize Value = todouble(count())\n| extend Metric = \"Backend calls\", Order = 5),\n(dependencies\n| where sdkVersion startswith \"apim:\" and success == false\n| summarize Value = todouble(count())\n| extend Metric = \"Backend failures\", Order = 6),\n(requests\n| where sdkVersion startswith \"apim:\"\n| summarize Value = todouble(dcount(coalesce(user_AuthenticatedId, user_Id)))\n| extend Metric = \"Known consumers\", Order = 7)\n| project Order, Metric, Value\n| sort by Order asc",
              "size": 3,
              "visualization": "tiles",
              "title": "APIM AI Gateway metrics",
              "tileSettings": {
                "leftContent": {
                  "columnMatch": "Value",
                  "formatter": 12,
                  "formatOptions": {
                    "palette": "blue"
                  }
                },
                "showBorder": true,
                "titleContent": {
                  "columnMatch": "Metric",
                  "formatter": 1
                }
              },
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.insights/components",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{APIMApplicationInsights}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "apim-kpi-appinsights",
            "conditionalVisibility": {
              "parameterName": "APIMTelemetrySource",
              "comparison": "isEqualTo",
              "value": "applicationInsights"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "#### Request and failure trend\n\nThe hourly trend separates total gateway demand from failed requests. Look for sudden traffic bursts, sustained failure growth, periodic automation, or failures that begin after a deployment or policy change. Correlate the affected time window with response codes, operations, backends, and Azure Activity. Sparse periods can reflect diagnostic sampling or ingestion delay."
            },
            "name": "apim-time-desc"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "AppRequests\n| where SDKVersion startswith \"apim:\"\n| summarize Requests = count(), Failures = countif(Success == false) by bin(TimeGenerated, 1h)\n| order by TimeGenerated asc",
              "size": 0,
              "visualization": "timechart",
              "title": "Gateway requests and failures over time",
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{APIMWorkspace}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "apim-time",
            "conditionalVisibility": {
              "parameterName": "APIMTelemetrySource",
              "comparison": "isEqualTo",
              "value": "workspace"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "requests\n| where sdkVersion startswith \"apim:\"\n| summarize Requests = count(), Failures = countif(success == false) by bin(timestamp, 1h)\n| order by timestamp asc",
              "size": 0,
              "visualization": "timechart",
              "title": "Gateway requests and failures over time",
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.insights/components",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{APIMApplicationInsights}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "apim-time-appinsights",
            "conditionalVisibility": {
              "parameterName": "APIMTelemetrySource",
              "comparison": "isEqualTo",
              "value": "applicationInsights"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "#### Behavioral request-volume anomaly\n\nReplicates `APIMAbnormalRequestVolume` by comparing the last hour per agent/caller and API with the preceding seven-day hourly median and p95. Select at least **7 days** in the workbook time range. The alert threshold is 50 current requests, 3x median, 1.5x p95, and at least six baseline hours; planned batch jobs and load tests can match."
            },
            "name": "apim-volume-anomaly-desc"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "let recentWindow=1h;\nlet baselineWindow=7d;\nlet Historical=AppRequests\n| where TimeGenerated between (ago(baselineWindow) .. ago(recentWindow))\n| where SDKVersion startswith \"apim:\" or tostring(Properties[\"Service Type\"]) =~ \"API Management\"\n| extend Caller=coalesce(UserAuthenticatedId, UserId, tostring(Properties[\"Subscription ID\"]), tostring(Properties[\"SubscriptionId\"]), tostring(Properties[\"subscriptionId\"]), ClientIP, \"unknown\"), APIName=coalesce(tostring(Properties[\"API Name\"]), Name)\n| extend AgentKey=coalesce(tostring(Properties[\"AgentId\"]), tostring(Properties[\"Agent ID\"]), tostring(Properties[\"ApplicationId\"]), tostring(Properties[\"Application ID\"]), AppRoleName, Caller)\n| summarize HourRequests=sum(ItemCount) by AgentKey, APIName, bin(TimeGenerated, 1h)\n| summarize BaselineMedian=percentile(HourRequests, 50), BaselineP95=percentile(HourRequests, 95), BaselineHours=count() by AgentKey, APIName;\nlet Current=AppRequests\n| where TimeGenerated > ago(recentWindow)\n| where SDKVersion startswith \"apim:\" or tostring(Properties[\"Service Type\"]) =~ \"API Management\"\n| extend Caller=coalesce(UserAuthenticatedId, UserId, tostring(Properties[\"Subscription ID\"]), tostring(Properties[\"SubscriptionId\"]), tostring(Properties[\"subscriptionId\"]), ClientIP, \"unknown\"), APIName=coalesce(tostring(Properties[\"API Name\"]), Name)\n| extend AgentKey=coalesce(tostring(Properties[\"AgentId\"]), tostring(Properties[\"Agent ID\"]), tostring(Properties[\"ApplicationId\"]), tostring(Properties[\"Application ID\"]), AppRoleName, Caller)\n| summarize CurrentRequests=sum(ItemCount), Operations=dcount(Name), FirstSeen=min(TimeGenerated), LastSeen=max(TimeGenerated), Caller=take_any(Caller), ClientIP=take_any(ClientIP) by AgentKey, APIName;\nCurrent\n| join kind=inner Historical on AgentKey, APIName\n| extend MedianRatio=round(todouble(CurrentRequests) / max_of(todouble(BaselineMedian), 1.0), 2), P95Ratio=round(todouble(CurrentRequests) / max_of(todouble(BaselineP95), 1.0), 2)\n| where BaselineHours >= 6 and CurrentRequests >= 50 and MedianRatio >= 3.0 and P95Ratio >= 1.5\n| project LastSeen, AgentKey, Caller, ClientIP, APIName, CurrentRequests, BaselineMedian, BaselineP95, MedianRatio, P95Ratio, BaselineHours, Operations, FirstSeen\n| order by MedianRatio desc",
              "size": 0,
              "title": "Abnormal API consumption against seven-day baseline",
              "gridSettings": {
                "formatters": [
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "MedianRatio",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "red"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "P95Ratio",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "yellow"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{APIMWorkspace}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "apim-volume-anomaly",
            "conditionalVisibility": {
              "parameterName": "APIMTelemetrySource",
              "comparison": "isEqualTo",
              "value": "workspace"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "let recentWindow=1h;\nlet baselineWindow=7d;\nlet Historical=requests\n| where timestamp between (ago(baselineWindow) .. ago(recentWindow))\n| where sdkVersion startswith \"apim:\" or tostring(customDimensions[\"Service Type\"]) =~ \"API Management\"\n| extend Caller=coalesce(user_AuthenticatedId, user_Id, tostring(customDimensions[\"Subscription ID\"]), tostring(customDimensions[\"SubscriptionId\"]), tostring(customDimensions[\"subscriptionId\"]), client_IP, \"unknown\"), APIName=coalesce(tostring(customDimensions[\"API Name\"]), name)\n| extend AgentKey=coalesce(tostring(customDimensions[\"AgentId\"]), tostring(customDimensions[\"Agent ID\"]), tostring(customDimensions[\"ApplicationId\"]), tostring(customDimensions[\"Application ID\"]), cloud_RoleName, Caller)\n| summarize HourRequests=sum(itemCount) by AgentKey, APIName, bin(timestamp, 1h)\n| summarize BaselineMedian=percentile(HourRequests, 50), BaselineP95=percentile(HourRequests, 95), BaselineHours=count() by AgentKey, APIName;\nlet Current=requests\n| where timestamp > ago(recentWindow)\n| where sdkVersion startswith \"apim:\" or tostring(customDimensions[\"Service Type\"]) =~ \"API Management\"\n| extend Caller=coalesce(user_AuthenticatedId, user_Id, tostring(customDimensions[\"Subscription ID\"]), tostring(customDimensions[\"SubscriptionId\"]), tostring(customDimensions[\"subscriptionId\"]), client_IP, \"unknown\"), APIName=coalesce(tostring(customDimensions[\"API Name\"]), name)\n| extend AgentKey=coalesce(tostring(customDimensions[\"AgentId\"]), tostring(customDimensions[\"Agent ID\"]), tostring(customDimensions[\"ApplicationId\"]), tostring(customDimensions[\"Application ID\"]), cloud_RoleName, Caller)\n| summarize CurrentRequests=sum(itemCount), Operations=dcount(name), FirstSeen=min(timestamp), LastSeen=max(timestamp), Caller=take_any(Caller), client_IP=take_any(client_IP) by AgentKey, APIName;\nCurrent\n| join kind=inner Historical on AgentKey, APIName\n| extend MedianRatio=round(todouble(CurrentRequests) / max_of(todouble(BaselineMedian), 1.0), 2), P95Ratio=round(todouble(CurrentRequests) / max_of(todouble(BaselineP95), 1.0), 2)\n| where BaselineHours >= 6 and CurrentRequests >= 50 and MedianRatio >= 3.0 and P95Ratio >= 1.5\n| project LastSeen, AgentKey, Caller, client_IP, APIName, CurrentRequests, BaselineMedian, BaselineP95, MedianRatio, P95Ratio, BaselineHours, Operations, FirstSeen\n| order by MedianRatio desc",
              "size": 0,
              "title": "Abnormal API consumption against seven-day baseline",
              "gridSettings": {
                "formatters": [
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "MedianRatio",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "red"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "P95Ratio",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "yellow"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.insights/components",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{APIMApplicationInsights}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "apim-volume-anomaly-appinsights",
            "conditionalVisibility": {
              "parameterName": "APIMTelemetrySource",
              "comparison": "isEqualTo",
              "value": "applicationInsights"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "#### First-seen API operation for a known agent or caller\n\nReplicates `APIMNewOperationFirstSeen`. Select at least **14 days** so the panel can compare the last hour with a meaningful history. It excludes entirely new agents/callers and requires two current calls. Review release and API change records before treating first use as access drift."
            },
            "name": "apim-new-operation-desc"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "let recentWindow=1h;\nlet baselineWindow=14d;\nlet Baseline=AppRequests\n| where TimeGenerated between (ago(baselineWindow) .. ago(recentWindow))\n| where SDKVersion startswith \"apim:\" or tostring(Properties[\"Service Type\"]) =~ \"API Management\"\n| extend Caller=coalesce(UserAuthenticatedId, UserId, tostring(Properties[\"Subscription ID\"]), tostring(Properties[\"SubscriptionId\"]), tostring(Properties[\"subscriptionId\"]), ClientIP, \"unknown\"), APIName=coalesce(tostring(Properties[\"API Name\"]), Name), Operation=coalesce(tostring(Properties[\"Operation Name\"]), Name)\n| extend AgentKey=coalesce(tostring(Properties[\"AgentId\"]), tostring(Properties[\"Agent ID\"]), tostring(Properties[\"ApplicationId\"]), tostring(Properties[\"Application ID\"]), AppRoleName, Caller)\n| distinct AgentKey, APIName, Operation;\nlet KnownAgents=Baseline | distinct AgentKey;\nlet Recent=AppRequests\n| where TimeGenerated > ago(recentWindow)\n| where SDKVersion startswith \"apim:\" or tostring(Properties[\"Service Type\"]) =~ \"API Management\"\n| extend Caller=coalesce(UserAuthenticatedId, UserId, tostring(Properties[\"Subscription ID\"]), tostring(Properties[\"SubscriptionId\"]), tostring(Properties[\"subscriptionId\"]), ClientIP, \"unknown\"), APIName=coalesce(tostring(Properties[\"API Name\"]), Name), Operation=coalesce(tostring(Properties[\"Operation Name\"]), Name)\n| extend AgentKey=coalesce(tostring(Properties[\"AgentId\"]), tostring(Properties[\"Agent ID\"]), tostring(Properties[\"ApplicationId\"]), tostring(Properties[\"Application ID\"]), AppRoleName, Caller);\nRecent\n| join kind=inner KnownAgents on AgentKey\n| join kind=leftanti Baseline on AgentKey, APIName, Operation\n| summarize Calls=sum(ItemCount), Failures=sum(iff(Success == false, ItemCount, 0)), ResultCodes=make_set(ResultCode, 10), FirstSeen=min(TimeGenerated), LastSeen=max(TimeGenerated), Caller=take_any(Caller), ClientIP=take_any(ClientIP), Country=take_any(ClientCountryOrRegion) by AgentKey, APIName, Operation\n| where Calls >= 2\n| extend FailureRate=round(100.0 * todouble(Failures) / max_of(todouble(Calls), 1.0), 2)\n| project LastSeen, AgentKey, Caller, ClientIP, Country, APIName, Operation, Calls, Failures, FailureRate, ResultCodes, FirstSeen\n| order by Calls desc",
              "size": 0,
              "title": "New API operation used by a known agent or caller",
              "gridSettings": {
                "formatters": [
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "FailureRate",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "red"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{APIMWorkspace}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "apim-new-operation",
            "conditionalVisibility": {
              "parameterName": "APIMTelemetrySource",
              "comparison": "isEqualTo",
              "value": "workspace"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "let recentWindow=1h;\nlet baselineWindow=14d;\nlet Baseline=requests\n| where timestamp between (ago(baselineWindow) .. ago(recentWindow))\n| where sdkVersion startswith \"apim:\" or tostring(customDimensions[\"Service Type\"]) =~ \"API Management\"\n| extend Caller=coalesce(user_AuthenticatedId, user_Id, tostring(customDimensions[\"Subscription ID\"]), tostring(customDimensions[\"SubscriptionId\"]), tostring(customDimensions[\"subscriptionId\"]), client_IP, \"unknown\"), APIName=coalesce(tostring(customDimensions[\"API Name\"]), name), Operation=coalesce(tostring(customDimensions[\"Operation Name\"]), name)\n| extend AgentKey=coalesce(tostring(customDimensions[\"AgentId\"]), tostring(customDimensions[\"Agent ID\"]), tostring(customDimensions[\"ApplicationId\"]), tostring(customDimensions[\"Application ID\"]), cloud_RoleName, Caller)\n| distinct AgentKey, APIName, Operation;\nlet KnownAgents=Baseline | distinct AgentKey;\nlet Recent=requests\n| where timestamp > ago(recentWindow)\n| where sdkVersion startswith \"apim:\" or tostring(customDimensions[\"Service Type\"]) =~ \"API Management\"\n| extend Caller=coalesce(user_AuthenticatedId, user_Id, tostring(customDimensions[\"Subscription ID\"]), tostring(customDimensions[\"SubscriptionId\"]), tostring(customDimensions[\"subscriptionId\"]), client_IP, \"unknown\"), APIName=coalesce(tostring(customDimensions[\"API Name\"]), name), Operation=coalesce(tostring(customDimensions[\"Operation Name\"]), name)\n| extend AgentKey=coalesce(tostring(customDimensions[\"AgentId\"]), tostring(customDimensions[\"Agent ID\"]), tostring(customDimensions[\"ApplicationId\"]), tostring(customDimensions[\"Application ID\"]), cloud_RoleName, Caller);\nRecent\n| join kind=inner KnownAgents on AgentKey\n| join kind=leftanti Baseline on AgentKey, APIName, Operation\n| summarize Calls=sum(itemCount), Failures=sum(iff(success == false, itemCount, 0)), ResultCodes=make_set(resultCode, 10), FirstSeen=min(timestamp), LastSeen=max(timestamp), Caller=take_any(Caller), client_IP=take_any(client_IP), Country=take_any(client_CountryOrRegion) by AgentKey, APIName, Operation\n| where Calls >= 2\n| extend FailureRate=round(100.0 * todouble(Failures) / max_of(todouble(Calls), 1.0), 2)\n| project LastSeen, AgentKey, Caller, client_IP, Country, APIName, Operation, Calls, Failures, FailureRate, ResultCodes, FirstSeen\n| order by Calls desc",
              "size": 0,
              "title": "New API operation used by a known agent or caller",
              "gridSettings": {
                "formatters": [
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "FailureRate",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "red"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.insights/components",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{APIMApplicationInsights}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "apim-new-operation-appinsights",
            "conditionalVisibility": {
              "parameterName": "APIMTelemetrySource",
              "comparison": "isEqualTo",
              "value": "applicationInsights"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "#### Geographic anomaly for a known agent or caller\n\nReplicates `APIMNewCountryForKnownCaller`. Select at least **14 days** and investigate only stable identities; VPNs, proxies, mobile users, and globally distributed applications commonly change location. Application Insights can retain derived country/city while masking `ClientIP` as `0.0.0.0`."
            },
            "name": "apim-new-country-desc"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "let recentWindow=1h;\nlet baselineWindow=14d;\nlet Baseline=AppRequests\n| where TimeGenerated between (ago(baselineWindow) .. ago(recentWindow))\n| where SDKVersion startswith \"apim:\" or tostring(Properties[\"Service Type\"]) =~ \"API Management\"\n| extend Caller=coalesce(UserAuthenticatedId, UserId, tostring(Properties[\"Subscription ID\"]), tostring(Properties[\"SubscriptionId\"]), tostring(Properties[\"subscriptionId\"]), ClientIP, \"unknown\"), Country=tostring(ClientCountryOrRegion)\n| extend AgentKey=coalesce(tostring(Properties[\"AgentId\"]), tostring(Properties[\"Agent ID\"]), tostring(Properties[\"ApplicationId\"]), tostring(Properties[\"Application ID\"]), AppRoleName, Caller)\n| where isnotempty(Country)\n| distinct AgentKey, Country;\nlet KnownAgents=Baseline | distinct AgentKey;\nAppRequests\n| where TimeGenerated > ago(recentWindow)\n| where SDKVersion startswith \"apim:\" or tostring(Properties[\"Service Type\"]) =~ \"API Management\"\n| extend Caller=coalesce(UserAuthenticatedId, UserId, tostring(Properties[\"Subscription ID\"]), tostring(Properties[\"SubscriptionId\"]), tostring(Properties[\"subscriptionId\"]), ClientIP, \"unknown\"), Country=tostring(ClientCountryOrRegion), City=tostring(ClientCity), APIName=coalesce(tostring(Properties[\"API Name\"]), Name)\n| extend AgentKey=coalesce(tostring(Properties[\"AgentId\"]), tostring(Properties[\"Agent ID\"]), tostring(Properties[\"ApplicationId\"]), tostring(Properties[\"Application ID\"]), AppRoleName, Caller)\n| where isnotempty(Country)\n| join kind=inner KnownAgents on AgentKey\n| join kind=leftanti Baseline on AgentKey, Country\n| summarize Requests=sum(ItemCount), APIs=make_set(APIName, 10), Operations=make_set(Name, 20), Cities=make_set(City, 10), FirstSeen=min(TimeGenerated), LastSeen=max(TimeGenerated), Caller=take_any(Caller), ClientIP=take_any(ClientIP) by AgentKey, Country\n| where Requests >= 3\n| project LastSeen, AgentKey, Caller, ClientIP, Country, Cities, Requests, APIs, Operations, FirstSeen\n| order by Requests desc",
              "size": 0,
              "title": "New country for a known APIM agent or caller",
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{APIMWorkspace}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "apim-new-country",
            "conditionalVisibility": {
              "parameterName": "APIMTelemetrySource",
              "comparison": "isEqualTo",
              "value": "workspace"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "let recentWindow=1h;\nlet baselineWindow=14d;\nlet Baseline=requests\n| where timestamp between (ago(baselineWindow) .. ago(recentWindow))\n| where sdkVersion startswith \"apim:\" or tostring(customDimensions[\"Service Type\"]) =~ \"API Management\"\n| extend Caller=coalesce(user_AuthenticatedId, user_Id, tostring(customDimensions[\"Subscription ID\"]), tostring(customDimensions[\"SubscriptionId\"]), tostring(customDimensions[\"subscriptionId\"]), client_IP, \"unknown\"), Country=tostring(client_CountryOrRegion)\n| extend AgentKey=coalesce(tostring(customDimensions[\"AgentId\"]), tostring(customDimensions[\"Agent ID\"]), tostring(customDimensions[\"ApplicationId\"]), tostring(customDimensions[\"Application ID\"]), cloud_RoleName, Caller)\n| where isnotempty(Country)\n| distinct AgentKey, Country;\nlet KnownAgents=Baseline | distinct AgentKey;\nrequests\n| where timestamp > ago(recentWindow)\n| where sdkVersion startswith \"apim:\" or tostring(customDimensions[\"Service Type\"]) =~ \"API Management\"\n| extend Caller=coalesce(user_AuthenticatedId, user_Id, tostring(customDimensions[\"Subscription ID\"]), tostring(customDimensions[\"SubscriptionId\"]), tostring(customDimensions[\"subscriptionId\"]), client_IP, \"unknown\"), Country=tostring(client_CountryOrRegion), City=tostring(client_City), APIName=coalesce(tostring(customDimensions[\"API Name\"]), name)\n| extend AgentKey=coalesce(tostring(customDimensions[\"AgentId\"]), tostring(customDimensions[\"Agent ID\"]), tostring(customDimensions[\"ApplicationId\"]), tostring(customDimensions[\"Application ID\"]), cloud_RoleName, Caller)\n| where isnotempty(Country)\n| join kind=inner KnownAgents on AgentKey\n| join kind=leftanti Baseline on AgentKey, Country\n| summarize Requests=sum(itemCount), APIs=make_set(APIName, 10), Operations=make_set(name, 20), Cities=make_set(City, 10), FirstSeen=min(timestamp), LastSeen=max(timestamp), Caller=take_any(Caller), client_IP=take_any(client_IP) by AgentKey, Country\n| where Requests >= 3\n| project LastSeen, AgentKey, Caller, client_IP, Country, Cities, Requests, APIs, Operations, FirstSeen\n| order by Requests desc",
              "size": 0,
              "title": "New country for a known APIM agent or caller",
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.insights/components",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{APIMApplicationInsights}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "apim-new-country-appinsights",
            "conditionalVisibility": {
              "parameterName": "APIMTelemetrySource",
              "comparison": "isEqualTo",
              "value": "applicationInsights"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "#### API operation performance\n\nThis table ranks API operations by request volume and reports failure percentage plus p50, p95, and p99 latency. Use p95/p99 to find tail-latency problems hidden by averages, then pivot to the backend and failure panels using the operation name. High latency can originate in APIM policy processing, network transit, backend execution, streaming duration, or cold starts."
            },
            "name": "apim-performance-desc"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "AppRequests\n| where SDKVersion startswith \"apim:\"\n| where \"{AgentSearch}\" == \"\" or Name has \"{AgentSearch}\" or Url has \"{AgentSearch}\"\n| summarize Requests = count(), Failures = countif(Success == false), AvgMs = round(avg(DurationMs), 0), P50Ms = round(percentile(DurationMs, 50), 0), P95Ms = round(percentile(DurationMs, 95), 0), P99Ms = round(percentile(DurationMs, 99), 0), LastSeen = max(TimeGenerated) by Operation = Name\n| extend FailurePct = round(100.0 * Failures / Requests, 2)\n| top 30 by Requests desc",
              "size": 0,
              "title": "API operations — volume, failure rate, and tail latency",
              "gridSettings": {
                "formatters": [
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "Requests",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "blue"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "FailurePct",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "red"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "P95Ms",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "yellow"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "P99Ms",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "red"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{APIMWorkspace}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "apim-performance",
            "conditionalVisibility": {
              "parameterName": "APIMTelemetrySource",
              "comparison": "isEqualTo",
              "value": "workspace"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "requests\n| where sdkVersion startswith \"apim:\"\n| where \"{AgentSearch}\" == \"\" or name has \"{AgentSearch}\" or url has \"{AgentSearch}\"\n| summarize Requests = count(), Failures = countif(success == false), AvgMs = round(avg(duration), 0), P50Ms = round(percentile(duration, 50), 0), P95Ms = round(percentile(duration, 95), 0), P99Ms = round(percentile(duration, 99), 0), LastSeen = max(timestamp) by Operation = name\n| extend FailurePct = round(100.0 * Failures / Requests, 2)\n| top 30 by Requests desc",
              "size": 0,
              "title": "API operations — volume, failure rate, and tail latency",
              "gridSettings": {
                "formatters": [
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "Requests",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "blue"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "FailurePct",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "red"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "P95Ms",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "yellow"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "P99Ms",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "red"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.insights/components",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{APIMApplicationInsights}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "apim-performance-appinsights",
            "conditionalVisibility": {
              "parameterName": "APIMTelemetrySource",
              "comparison": "isEqualTo",
              "value": "applicationInsights"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "#### Tail-latency anomaly against baseline\n\nMirrors the `APIMLatencyBaselineAnomaly` hunt by comparing the current operation p95 with the preceding seven-day hourly distribution. Select at least **7 days**. Results require 10 current requests, p95 of at least one second, 1.5x baseline, and six baseline hours. Treat this as investigation evidence, not proof of attack."
            },
            "name": "apim-latency-anomaly-desc"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "let recentWindow=1h;\nlet baselineWindow=7d;\nlet Historical=AppRequests\n| where TimeGenerated between (ago(baselineWindow) .. ago(recentWindow))\n| where SDKVersion startswith \"apim:\" or tostring(Properties[\"Service Type\"]) =~ \"API Management\"\n| extend APIName=coalesce(tostring(Properties[\"API Name\"]), Name), Operation=coalesce(tostring(Properties[\"Operation Name\"]), Name)\n| summarize HourP95=percentile(DurationMs, 95), HourRequests=sum(ItemCount) by APIName, Operation, bin(TimeGenerated, 1h)\n| summarize BaselineP95=percentile(HourP95, 50), HistoricalTailP95=percentile(HourP95, 95), BaselineHours=count() by APIName, Operation;\nAppRequests\n| where TimeGenerated > ago(recentWindow)\n| where SDKVersion startswith \"apim:\" or tostring(Properties[\"Service Type\"]) =~ \"API Management\"\n| extend APIName=coalesce(tostring(Properties[\"API Name\"]), Name), Operation=coalesce(tostring(Properties[\"Operation Name\"]), Name)\n| summarize CurrentRequests=sum(ItemCount), CurrentP95=percentile(DurationMs, 95), CurrentP99=percentile(DurationMs, 99), Failures=sum(iff(Success == false, ItemCount, 0)), LastSeen=max(TimeGenerated) by APIName, Operation\n| join kind=inner Historical on APIName, Operation\n| extend P95Ratio=round(CurrentP95 / max_of(BaselineP95, 1.0), 2), FailureRate=round(100.0 * todouble(Failures) / max_of(todouble(CurrentRequests), 1.0), 2)\n| where BaselineHours >= 6 and CurrentRequests >= 10 and CurrentP95 >= 1000 and P95Ratio >= 1.5\n| project LastSeen, APIName, Operation, CurrentRequests, CurrentP95, CurrentP99, BaselineP95, HistoricalTailP95, P95Ratio, Failures, FailureRate, BaselineHours\n| order by P95Ratio desc",
              "size": 0,
              "title": "Tail-latency anomaly against seven-day baseline",
              "gridSettings": {
                "formatters": [
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "P95Ratio",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "red"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "FailureRate",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "yellow"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{APIMWorkspace}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "apim-latency-anomaly",
            "conditionalVisibility": {
              "parameterName": "APIMTelemetrySource",
              "comparison": "isEqualTo",
              "value": "workspace"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "let recentWindow=1h;\nlet baselineWindow=7d;\nlet Historical=requests\n| where timestamp between (ago(baselineWindow) .. ago(recentWindow))\n| where sdkVersion startswith \"apim:\" or tostring(customDimensions[\"Service Type\"]) =~ \"API Management\"\n| extend APIName=coalesce(tostring(customDimensions[\"API Name\"]), name), Operation=coalesce(tostring(customDimensions[\"Operation Name\"]), name)\n| summarize HourP95=percentile(duration, 95), HourRequests=sum(itemCount) by APIName, Operation, bin(timestamp, 1h)\n| summarize BaselineP95=percentile(HourP95, 50), HistoricalTailP95=percentile(HourP95, 95), BaselineHours=count() by APIName, Operation;\nrequests\n| where timestamp > ago(recentWindow)\n| where sdkVersion startswith \"apim:\" or tostring(customDimensions[\"Service Type\"]) =~ \"API Management\"\n| extend APIName=coalesce(tostring(customDimensions[\"API Name\"]), name), Operation=coalesce(tostring(customDimensions[\"Operation Name\"]), name)\n| summarize CurrentRequests=sum(itemCount), CurrentP95=percentile(duration, 95), CurrentP99=percentile(duration, 99), Failures=sum(iff(success == false, itemCount, 0)), LastSeen=max(timestamp) by APIName, Operation\n| join kind=inner Historical on APIName, Operation\n| extend P95Ratio=round(CurrentP95 / max_of(BaselineP95, 1.0), 2), FailureRate=round(100.0 * todouble(Failures) / max_of(todouble(CurrentRequests), 1.0), 2)\n| where BaselineHours >= 6 and CurrentRequests >= 10 and CurrentP95 >= 1000 and P95Ratio >= 1.5\n| project LastSeen, APIName, Operation, CurrentRequests, CurrentP95, CurrentP99, BaselineP95, HistoricalTailP95, P95Ratio, Failures, FailureRate, BaselineHours\n| order by P95Ratio desc",
              "size": 0,
              "title": "Tail-latency anomaly against seven-day baseline",
              "gridSettings": {
                "formatters": [
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "P95Ratio",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "red"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "FailureRate",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "yellow"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.insights/components",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{APIMApplicationInsights}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "apim-latency-anomaly-appinsights",
            "conditionalVisibility": {
              "parameterName": "APIMTelemetrySource",
              "comparison": "isEqualTo",
              "value": "applicationInsights"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "#### HTTP response-code distribution\n\nResponse codes show the outcome mix seen by callers. `2xx` indicates accepted/successful traffic, `4xx` usually points to caller input, authentication, authorization, policy, or route issues, and `5xx` indicates gateway or backend failure. Interpret codes with the API contract: some APIs legitimately use `202`, `206`, `401`, or `404` in normal workflows."
            },
            "name": "apim-status-desc"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "AppRequests\n| where SDKVersion startswith \"apim:\"\n| summarize Requests = count() by ResultCode\n| order by Requests desc",
              "size": 1,
              "visualization": "piechart",
              "title": "HTTP response codes",
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{APIMWorkspace}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "apim-status",
            "conditionalVisibility": {
              "parameterName": "APIMTelemetrySource",
              "comparison": "isEqualTo",
              "value": "workspace"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "requests\n| where sdkVersion startswith \"apim:\"\n| summarize Requests = count() by resultCode\n| order by Requests desc",
              "size": 1,
              "visualization": "piechart",
              "title": "HTTP response codes",
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.insights/components",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{APIMApplicationInsights}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "apim-status-appinsights",
            "conditionalVisibility": {
              "parameterName": "APIMTelemetrySource",
              "comparison": "isEqualTo",
              "value": "applicationInsights"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "### 🔀 Backends, consumers, and reliability\n\nThese panels explain where APIM forwards traffic, who is consuming it, and which gateway or backend transactions failed. Use them together to separate a problematic client or subscription from a degraded downstream service."
            },
            "name": "apim-h2"
          },
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "#### Backend routes and dependencies\n\nThis table groups APIM dependency telemetry by backend target and operation, with call volume, failures, average latency, p95 latency, and last-seen time. A healthy gateway with a slow or failing backend isolates the problem downstream. Empty results can mean the API returned from policy without forwarding, backend diagnostics aren't enabled, or telemetry hasn't arrived."
            },
            "name": "apim-backends-desc"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "AppDependencies\n| where SDKVersion startswith \"apim:\"\n| where \"{AgentSearch}\" == \"\" or Name has \"{AgentSearch}\" or Target has \"{AgentSearch}\"\n| summarize Calls = count(), Failures = countif(Success == false), AvgMs = round(avg(DurationMs), 0), P95Ms = round(percentile(DurationMs, 95), 0), LastSeen = max(TimeGenerated) by Backend = Target, Dependency = Name\n| extend FailurePct = round(100.0 * Failures / Calls, 2)\n| top 30 by Calls desc",
              "size": 0,
              "title": "Backend routes — calls, failures, and latency",
              "gridSettings": {
                "formatters": [
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "Calls",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "blue"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "FailurePct",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "red"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "P95Ms",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "yellow"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{APIMWorkspace}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "apim-backends",
            "conditionalVisibility": {
              "parameterName": "APIMTelemetrySource",
              "comparison": "isEqualTo",
              "value": "workspace"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "dependencies\n| where sdkVersion startswith \"apim:\"\n| where \"{AgentSearch}\" == \"\" or name has \"{AgentSearch}\" or target has \"{AgentSearch}\"\n| summarize Calls = count(), Failures = countif(success == false), AvgMs = round(avg(duration), 0), P95Ms = round(percentile(duration, 95), 0), LastSeen = max(timestamp) by Backend = target, Dependency = name\n| extend FailurePct = round(100.0 * Failures / Calls, 2)\n| top 30 by Calls desc",
              "size": 0,
              "title": "Backend routes — calls, failures, and latency",
              "gridSettings": {
                "formatters": [
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "Calls",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "blue"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "FailurePct",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "red"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "P95Ms",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "yellow"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.insights/components",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{APIMApplicationInsights}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "apim-backends-appinsights",
            "conditionalVisibility": {
              "parameterName": "APIMTelemetrySource",
              "comparison": "isEqualTo",
              "value": "applicationInsights"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "#### Consumer and subscription attribution\n\nThis view attributes request volume, failures, operation breadth, and p95 latency to the best available authenticated user, anonymous user, or APIM subscription identifier. Use separate runtime keys or identities per application/environment for meaningful ownership and quota analysis. `anonymous / unknown` means attribution wasn't populated; do not infer that the request was unauthenticated without checking the API policy."
            },
            "name": "apim-consumers-desc"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "AppRequests\n| where SDKVersion startswith \"apim:\"\n      | extend Consumer = coalesce(UserAuthenticatedId, UserId, tostring(Properties[\"Subscription ID\"]), tostring(Properties[\"SubscriptionId\"]), tostring(Properties[\"subscriptionId\"]), \"anonymous / unknown\")\n| where \"{AgentSearch}\" == \"\" or Consumer has \"{AgentSearch}\" or Name has \"{AgentSearch}\"\n| summarize Requests = count(), Failures = countif(Success == false), Operations = dcount(Name), P95Ms = round(percentile(DurationMs, 95), 0), LastSeen = max(TimeGenerated) by Consumer\n| extend FailurePct = round(100.0 * Failures / Requests, 2)\n| top 30 by Requests desc",
              "size": 0,
              "title": "Consumers / subscriptions — gateway usage",
              "gridSettings": {
                "formatters": [
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "Requests",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "blue"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "FailurePct",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "red"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "P95Ms",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "yellow"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{APIMWorkspace}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "apim-consumers",
            "conditionalVisibility": {
              "parameterName": "APIMTelemetrySource",
              "comparison": "isEqualTo",
              "value": "workspace"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "requests\n| where sdkVersion startswith \"apim:\"\n      | extend Consumer = coalesce(user_AuthenticatedId, user_Id, tostring(customDimensions[\"Subscription ID\"]), tostring(customDimensions[\"SubscriptionId\"]), tostring(customDimensions[\"subscriptionId\"]), \"anonymous / unknown\")\n| where \"{AgentSearch}\" == \"\" or Consumer has \"{AgentSearch}\" or name has \"{AgentSearch}\"\n| summarize Requests = count(), Failures = countif(success == false), Operations = dcount(name), P95Ms = round(percentile(duration, 95), 0), LastSeen = max(timestamp) by Consumer\n| extend FailurePct = round(100.0 * Failures / Requests, 2)\n| top 30 by Requests desc",
              "size": 0,
              "title": "Consumers / subscriptions — gateway usage",
              "gridSettings": {
                "formatters": [
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "Requests",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "blue"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "FailurePct",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "red"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "P95Ms",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "yellow"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.insights/components",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{APIMApplicationInsights}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "apim-consumers-appinsights",
            "conditionalVisibility": {
              "parameterName": "APIMTelemetrySource",
              "comparison": "isEqualTo",
              "value": "applicationInsights"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "#### Unusual operation combination by agent or application\n\nMirrors `APIMUnusualOperationCombination`: a known agent/caller uses at least five operations and combines that breadth with two new operations or a state-changing operation in the last hour. Select at least **14 days**. This is behavioral context; validate intended workflows and authorization."
            },
            "name": "apim-operation-combination-desc"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "let recentWindow=1h;\nlet baselineWindow=14d;\nlet sensitiveVerbs=dynamic([\"admin\", \"export\", \"delete\", \"remove\", \"drop\", \"update\", \"patch\", \"create\", \"disable\", \"reset\", \"grant\", \"revoke\", \"purge\", \"write\", \"send\"]);\nlet Baseline=AppRequests\n| where TimeGenerated between (ago(baselineWindow) .. ago(recentWindow))\n| where SDKVersion startswith \"apim:\" or tostring(Properties[\"Service Type\"]) =~ \"API Management\"\n| extend Caller=coalesce(UserAuthenticatedId, UserId, tostring(Properties[\"Subscription ID\"]), tostring(Properties[\"SubscriptionId\"]), tostring(Properties[\"subscriptionId\"]), ClientIP, \"unknown\"), Operation=tolower(coalesce(tostring(Properties[\"Operation Name\"]), Name))\n| extend AgentKey=coalesce(tostring(Properties[\"AgentId\"]), tostring(Properties[\"Agent ID\"]), tostring(Properties[\"ApplicationId\"]), tostring(Properties[\"Application ID\"]), AppRoleName, Caller)\n| distinct AgentKey, Operation;\nlet Recent=AppRequests\n| where TimeGenerated > ago(recentWindow)\n| where SDKVersion startswith \"apim:\" or tostring(Properties[\"Service Type\"]) =~ \"API Management\"\n| extend Caller=coalesce(UserAuthenticatedId, UserId, tostring(Properties[\"Subscription ID\"]), tostring(Properties[\"SubscriptionId\"]), tostring(Properties[\"subscriptionId\"]), ClientIP, \"unknown\"), APIName=coalesce(tostring(Properties[\"API Name\"]), Name), Operation=tolower(coalesce(tostring(Properties[\"Operation Name\"]), Name))\n| extend AgentKey=coalesce(tostring(Properties[\"AgentId\"]), tostring(Properties[\"Agent ID\"]), tostring(Properties[\"ApplicationId\"]), tostring(Properties[\"Application ID\"]), AppRoleName, Caller);\nlet NewOperations=Recent\n| join kind=leftanti Baseline on AgentKey, Operation\n| summarize NewOperationCount=dcount(Operation), NewOperations=make_set(Operation, 25) by AgentKey;\nRecent\n| summarize Requests=sum(ItemCount), DistinctOperations=dcount(Operation), Operations=make_set(Operation, 50), SensitiveOperations=make_set_if(Operation, Operation has_any (sensitiveVerbs), 25), APIs=make_set(APIName, 15), Failures=sum(iff(Success == false, ItemCount, 0)), FirstSeen=min(TimeGenerated), LastSeen=max(TimeGenerated), Caller=take_any(Caller), ClientIP=take_any(ClientIP) by AgentKey\n| extend SensitiveOperationCount=array_length(SensitiveOperations)\n| join kind=leftouter NewOperations on AgentKey\n| extend NewOperationCount=coalesce(NewOperationCount, 0), NewOperations=coalesce(NewOperations, dynamic([]))\n| where DistinctOperations >= 5 and (NewOperationCount >= 2 or SensitiveOperationCount >= 1)\n| extend FailureRate=round(100.0 * todouble(Failures) / max_of(todouble(Requests), 1.0), 2)\n| project LastSeen, AgentKey, Caller, ClientIP, Requests, DistinctOperations, NewOperationCount, NewOperations, SensitiveOperationCount, SensitiveOperations, APIs, Operations, Failures, FailureRate, FirstSeen\n| order by NewOperationCount desc, DistinctOperations desc",
              "size": 0,
              "title": "Broad, new, or state-changing operation combinations",
              "gridSettings": {
                "formatters": [
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "NewOperationCount",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "red"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "SensitiveOperationCount",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "yellow"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{APIMWorkspace}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "apim-operation-combination",
            "conditionalVisibility": {
              "parameterName": "APIMTelemetrySource",
              "comparison": "isEqualTo",
              "value": "workspace"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "let recentWindow=1h;\nlet baselineWindow=14d;\nlet sensitiveVerbs=dynamic([\"admin\", \"export\", \"delete\", \"remove\", \"drop\", \"update\", \"patch\", \"create\", \"disable\", \"reset\", \"grant\", \"revoke\", \"purge\", \"write\", \"send\"]);\nlet Baseline=requests\n| where timestamp between (ago(baselineWindow) .. ago(recentWindow))\n| where sdkVersion startswith \"apim:\" or tostring(customDimensions[\"Service Type\"]) =~ \"API Management\"\n| extend Caller=coalesce(user_AuthenticatedId, user_Id, tostring(customDimensions[\"Subscription ID\"]), tostring(customDimensions[\"SubscriptionId\"]), tostring(customDimensions[\"subscriptionId\"]), client_IP, \"unknown\"), Operation=tolower(coalesce(tostring(customDimensions[\"Operation Name\"]), name))\n| extend AgentKey=coalesce(tostring(customDimensions[\"AgentId\"]), tostring(customDimensions[\"Agent ID\"]), tostring(customDimensions[\"ApplicationId\"]), tostring(customDimensions[\"Application ID\"]), cloud_RoleName, Caller)\n| distinct AgentKey, Operation;\nlet Recent=requests\n| where timestamp > ago(recentWindow)\n| where sdkVersion startswith \"apim:\" or tostring(customDimensions[\"Service Type\"]) =~ \"API Management\"\n| extend Caller=coalesce(user_AuthenticatedId, user_Id, tostring(customDimensions[\"Subscription ID\"]), tostring(customDimensions[\"SubscriptionId\"]), tostring(customDimensions[\"subscriptionId\"]), client_IP, \"unknown\"), APIName=coalesce(tostring(customDimensions[\"API Name\"]), name), Operation=tolower(coalesce(tostring(customDimensions[\"Operation Name\"]), name))\n| extend AgentKey=coalesce(tostring(customDimensions[\"AgentId\"]), tostring(customDimensions[\"Agent ID\"]), tostring(customDimensions[\"ApplicationId\"]), tostring(customDimensions[\"Application ID\"]), cloud_RoleName, Caller);\nlet NewOperations=Recent\n| join kind=leftanti Baseline on AgentKey, Operation\n| summarize NewOperationCount=dcount(Operation), NewOperations=make_set(Operation, 25) by AgentKey;\nRecent\n| summarize Requests=sum(itemCount), DistinctOperations=dcount(Operation), Operations=make_set(Operation, 50), SensitiveOperations=make_set_if(Operation, Operation has_any (sensitiveVerbs), 25), APIs=make_set(APIName, 15), Failures=sum(iff(success == false, itemCount, 0)), FirstSeen=min(timestamp), LastSeen=max(timestamp), Caller=take_any(Caller), client_IP=take_any(client_IP) by AgentKey\n| extend SensitiveOperationCount=array_length(SensitiveOperations)\n| join kind=leftouter NewOperations on AgentKey\n| extend NewOperationCount=coalesce(NewOperationCount, 0), NewOperations=coalesce(NewOperations, dynamic([]))\n| where DistinctOperations >= 5 and (NewOperationCount >= 2 or SensitiveOperationCount >= 1)\n| extend FailureRate=round(100.0 * todouble(Failures) / max_of(todouble(Requests), 1.0), 2)\n| project LastSeen, AgentKey, Caller, client_IP, Requests, DistinctOperations, NewOperationCount, NewOperations, SensitiveOperationCount, SensitiveOperations, APIs, Operations, Failures, FailureRate, FirstSeen\n| order by NewOperationCount desc, DistinctOperations desc",
              "size": 0,
              "title": "Broad, new, or state-changing operation combinations",
              "gridSettings": {
                "formatters": [
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "NewOperationCount",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "red"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "SensitiveOperationCount",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "yellow"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.insights/components",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{APIMApplicationInsights}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "apim-operation-combination-appinsights",
            "conditionalVisibility": {
              "parameterName": "APIMTelemetrySource",
              "comparison": "isEqualTo",
              "value": "applicationInsights"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "#### Gateway and backend failure events\n\nThis event feed combines failed frontend requests and failed backend dependencies. `Layer` identifies whether the caller-facing gateway transaction or downstream call failed; `OperationId` is the investigation pivot into related requests, dependencies, traces, exceptions, and agent spans. A single logical failure can create records in both layers, so don't add the two counts as independent incidents."
            },
            "name": "apim-errors-desc"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "union isfuzzy=true\n(AppRequests\n| where SDKVersion startswith \"apim:\" and Success == false\n| project TimeGenerated, Layer = \"Gateway\", OperationId, Operation = Name, Target = Url, ResultCode, DurationMs),\n(AppDependencies\n| where SDKVersion startswith \"apim:\" and Success == false\n| project TimeGenerated, Layer = \"Backend\", OperationId, Operation = Name, Target, ResultCode, DurationMs)\n| order by TimeGenerated desc\n| take 100",
              "size": 0,
              "title": "Recent gateway and backend failures",
              "gridSettings": {
                "formatters": [
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "Layer",
                    "formatter": 0
                  },
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "DurationMs",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "red"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{APIMWorkspace}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "apim-errors",
            "conditionalVisibility": {
              "parameterName": "APIMTelemetrySource",
              "comparison": "isEqualTo",
              "value": "workspace"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "union isfuzzy=true\n(requests\n| where sdkVersion startswith \"apim:\" and success == false\n| project timestamp, Layer = \"Gateway\", operation_Id, Operation = name, target = url, resultCode, duration),\n(dependencies\n| where sdkVersion startswith \"apim:\" and success == false\n| project timestamp, Layer = \"Backend\", operation_Id, Operation = name, target, resultCode, duration)\n| order by timestamp desc\n| take 100",
              "size": 0,
              "title": "Recent gateway and backend failures",
              "gridSettings": {
                "formatters": [
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "Layer",
                    "formatter": 0
                  },
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "duration",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "red"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.insights/components",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{APIMApplicationInsights}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "apim-errors-appinsights",
            "conditionalVisibility": {
              "parameterName": "APIMTelemetrySource",
              "comparison": "isEqualTo",
              "value": "applicationInsights"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "#### Request to dependency correlation\n\nMirrors `APIMRequestDependencyCorrelation` and joins APIM frontend requests with downstream dependencies through `OperationId`. Use it to reconstruct request-to-backend flow, isolate a failing dependency, and connect the gateway transaction with agent/model/tool spans when those dimensions are emitted."
            },
            "name": "apim-request-dependency-desc"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "let Requests=AppRequests\n| where TimeGenerated > ago(24h)\n| where SDKVersion startswith \"apim:\" or tostring(Properties[\"Service Type\"]) =~ \"API Management\"\n| extend Caller=coalesce(UserAuthenticatedId, UserId, tostring(Properties[\"Subscription ID\"]), tostring(Properties[\"SubscriptionId\"]), tostring(Properties[\"subscriptionId\"]), ClientIP, \"unknown\"), APIName=coalesce(tostring(Properties[\"API Name\"]), Name), RequestId=tostring(Properties[\"Request Id\"])\n| project RequestTime=TimeGenerated, OperationId, RequestId, Caller, ClientIP, APIName, RequestOperation=Name, RequestUrl=Url, RequestResult=ResultCode, RequestSuccess=Success, RequestDurationMs=DurationMs;\nlet Dependencies=AppDependencies\n| where TimeGenerated > ago(24h)\n| project DependencyTime=TimeGenerated, OperationId, DependencyName=Name, DependencyTarget=Target, DependencyResult=ResultCode, DependencySuccess=Success, DependencyDurationMs=DurationMs, DependencyType, Agent=tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.agent.name\"]), Model=tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.request.model\"]), Tool=tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.tool.name\"]);\nRequests\n| join kind=inner Dependencies on OperationId\n| project RequestTime, DependencyTime, OperationId, RequestId, Caller, ClientIP, APIName, RequestOperation, RequestUrl, RequestResult, RequestSuccess, RequestDurationMs, DependencyName, DependencyTarget, DependencyType, DependencyResult, DependencySuccess, DependencyDurationMs, Agent, Model, Tool\n| order by RequestTime desc, DependencyTime asc\n| take 500",
              "size": 0,
              "title": "APIM requests correlated with downstream dependencies",
              "gridSettings": {
                "formatters": [
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "RequestDurationMs",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "yellow"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "DependencyDurationMs",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "yellow"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{APIMWorkspace}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "apim-request-dependency",
            "conditionalVisibility": {
              "parameterName": "APIMTelemetrySource",
              "comparison": "isEqualTo",
              "value": "workspace"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "let Requests=requests\n| where timestamp > ago(24h)\n| where sdkVersion startswith \"apim:\" or tostring(customDimensions[\"Service Type\"]) =~ \"API Management\"\n| extend Caller=coalesce(user_AuthenticatedId, user_Id, tostring(customDimensions[\"Subscription ID\"]), tostring(customDimensions[\"SubscriptionId\"]), tostring(customDimensions[\"subscriptionId\"]), client_IP, \"unknown\"), APIName=coalesce(tostring(customDimensions[\"API Name\"]), name), RequestId=tostring(customDimensions[\"Request Id\"])\n| project RequestTime=timestamp, operation_Id, RequestId, Caller, client_IP, APIName, RequestOperation=name, RequestUrl=url, RequestResult=resultCode, RequestSuccess=success, RequestDurationMs=duration;\nlet Dependencies=dependencies\n| where timestamp > ago(24h)\n| project DependencyTime=timestamp, operation_Id, DependencyName=name, DependencyTarget=target, DependencyResult=resultCode, DependencySuccess=success, DependencyDurationMs=duration, type, Agent=tostring(customDimensions[\"gen_ai.agent.name\"]), Model=tostring(customDimensions[\"gen_ai.request.model\"]), Tool=tostring(customDimensions[\"gen_ai.tool.name\"]);\nRequests\n| join kind=inner Dependencies on operation_Id\n| project RequestTime, DependencyTime, operation_Id, RequestId, Caller, client_IP, APIName, RequestOperation, RequestUrl, RequestResult, RequestSuccess, RequestDurationMs, DependencyName, DependencyTarget, type, DependencyResult, DependencySuccess, DependencyDurationMs, Agent, Model, Tool\n| order by RequestTime desc, DependencyTime asc\n| take 500",
              "size": 0,
              "title": "APIM requests correlated with downstream dependencies",
              "gridSettings": {
                "formatters": [
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "RequestDurationMs",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "yellow"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "DependencyDurationMs",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "yellow"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.insights/components",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{APIMApplicationInsights}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "apim-request-dependency-appinsights",
            "conditionalVisibility": {
              "parameterName": "APIMTelemetrySource",
              "comparison": "isEqualTo",
              "value": "applicationInsights"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "#### Failed request to exception correlation\n\nMirrors `APIMRequestExceptionCorrelation` by joining failed APIM frontend requests with Application Insights exceptions through `OperationId`. Exceptions support root-cause investigation but are not automatically security incidents. Empty results can mean no exception, sampling, or exception diagnostics are absent."
            },
            "name": "apim-request-exception-desc"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "let Requests=AppRequests\n| where TimeGenerated > ago(24h)\n| where SDKVersion startswith \"apim:\" or tostring(Properties[\"Service Type\"]) =~ \"API Management\"\n| where Success == false or toint(ResultCode) >= 400\n| extend Caller=coalesce(UserAuthenticatedId, UserId, tostring(Properties[\"Subscription ID\"]), tostring(Properties[\"SubscriptionId\"]), tostring(Properties[\"subscriptionId\"]), ClientIP, \"unknown\"), APIName=coalesce(tostring(Properties[\"API Name\"]), Name), RequestId=tostring(Properties[\"Request Id\"])\n| project RequestTime=TimeGenerated, OperationId, RequestId, Caller, ClientIP, APIName, RequestOperation=Name, RequestUrl=Url, RequestResult=ResultCode, RequestDurationMs=DurationMs;\nlet Exceptions=AppExceptions\n| where TimeGenerated > ago(24h)\n| extend ExceptionType=tostring(column_ifexists('Type', column_ifexists('type', ''))), ExceptionMessage=coalesce(tostring(column_ifexists('OuterMessage', column_ifexists('outerMessage', ''))), tostring(column_ifexists('InnermostMessage', column_ifexists('innermostMessage', ''))), tostring(column_ifexists('Message', column_ifexists('message', '')))), ExceptionMethod=tostring(column_ifexists('Method', column_ifexists('method', '')))\n| project ExceptionTime=TimeGenerated, OperationId, ExceptionType, ExceptionMessage, ExceptionMethod, ProblemId;\nRequests\n| join kind=inner Exceptions on OperationId\n| project RequestTime, ExceptionTime, OperationId, RequestId, Caller, ClientIP, APIName, RequestOperation, RequestUrl, RequestResult, RequestDurationMs, ExceptionType, ExceptionMessage, ExceptionMethod, ProblemId\n| order by RequestTime desc, ExceptionTime asc\n| take 250",
              "size": 0,
              "title": "Failed APIM requests correlated with exceptions",
              "gridSettings": {
                "formatters": [
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "RequestDurationMs",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "red"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{APIMWorkspace}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "apim-request-exception",
            "conditionalVisibility": {
              "parameterName": "APIMTelemetrySource",
              "comparison": "isEqualTo",
              "value": "workspace"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "let Requests=requests\n| where timestamp > ago(24h)\n| where sdkVersion startswith \"apim:\" or tostring(customDimensions[\"Service Type\"]) =~ \"API Management\"\n| where success == false or toint(resultCode) >= 400\n| extend Caller=coalesce(user_AuthenticatedId, user_Id, tostring(customDimensions[\"Subscription ID\"]), tostring(customDimensions[\"SubscriptionId\"]), tostring(customDimensions[\"subscriptionId\"]), client_IP, \"unknown\"), APIName=coalesce(tostring(customDimensions[\"API Name\"]), name), RequestId=tostring(customDimensions[\"Request Id\"])\n| project RequestTime=timestamp, operation_Id, RequestId, Caller, client_IP, APIName, RequestOperation=name, RequestUrl=url, RequestResult=resultCode, RequestDurationMs=duration;\nlet Exceptions=exceptions\n| where timestamp > ago(24h)\n| extend type=tostring(column_ifexists('Type', column_ifexists('type', ''))), ExceptionMessage=coalesce(tostring(column_ifexists('OuterMessage', column_ifexists('outerMessage', ''))), tostring(column_ifexists('InnermostMessage', column_ifexists('innermostMessage', ''))), tostring(column_ifexists('Message', column_ifexists('message', '')))), ExceptionMethod=tostring(column_ifexists('Method', column_ifexists('method', '')))\n| project ExceptionTime=timestamp, operation_Id, type, ExceptionMessage, ExceptionMethod, problemId;\nRequests\n| join kind=inner Exceptions on operation_Id\n| project RequestTime, ExceptionTime, operation_Id, RequestId, Caller, client_IP, APIName, RequestOperation, RequestUrl, RequestResult, RequestDurationMs, type, ExceptionMessage, ExceptionMethod, problemId\n| order by RequestTime desc, ExceptionTime asc\n| take 250",
              "size": 0,
              "title": "Failed APIM requests correlated with exceptions",
              "gridSettings": {
                "formatters": [
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "RequestDurationMs",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "red"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.insights/components",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{APIMApplicationInsights}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "apim-request-exception-appinsights",
            "conditionalVisibility": {
              "parameterName": "APIMTelemetrySource",
              "comparison": "isEqualTo",
              "value": "applicationInsights"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "### 🩺 Request and exception diagnostics\n\nThese scenarios turn `AppRequests` and `AppExceptions` into an operational triage path: identify recurring exception signatures, quantify their caller and route impact, isolate timeout/deadline failures, find release- or instance-specific regressions, and expose failed requests that have no correlated exception evidence. Correlation uses W3C `OperationId`; counts use `ItemCount` so sampled telemetry is represented correctly."
            },
            "name": "apim-app-telemetry-h"
          },
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "#### Correlated exception trend\n\nShows exception volume over time for operations observed at the APIM gateway, split by the deepest available exception type. A new series or sudden rise is a strong regression signal; a flat chart with failed requests elsewhere can mean failures are policy-generated, exceptions are sampled or handled without telemetry, or trace context is broken."
            },
            "name": "apim-exception-trend-desc"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "let ApimOperations=AppRequests\n| where SDKVersion startswith \"apim:\" or tostring(Properties[\"Service Type\"]) =~ \"API Management\"\n| extend Caller=coalesce(UserAuthenticatedId, UserId, tostring(Properties[\"Subscription ID\"]), tostring(Properties[\"SubscriptionId\"]), tostring(Properties[\"subscriptionId\"]), ClientIP, \"unknown\"), APIName=coalesce(tostring(Properties[\"API Name\"]), Name), RequestOperation=coalesce(tostring(Properties[\"Operation Name\"]), Name)\n| where \"{AgentSearch}\" == \"\" or Caller has \"{AgentSearch}\" or APIName has \"{AgentSearch}\" or RequestOperation has \"{AgentSearch}\"\n| distinct OperationId;\nAppExceptions\n| extend RootType=coalesce(InnermostType, ExceptionType, OuterType, \"unknown\"), ExceptionWeight=coalesce(tolong(ItemCount), 1)\n| join kind=inner ApimOperations on OperationId\n| summarize Exceptions=sum(ExceptionWeight), AffectedOperations=dcount(OperationId) by bin(TimeGenerated, 1h), RootType\n| order by TimeGenerated asc",
              "size": 0,
              "visualization": "timechart",
              "title": "Correlated APIM exception volume by root type",
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{APIMWorkspace}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "apim-exception-trend",
            "conditionalVisibility": {
              "parameterName": "APIMTelemetrySource",
              "comparison": "isEqualTo",
              "value": "workspace"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "let ApimOperations=requests\n| where sdkVersion startswith \"apim:\" or tostring(customDimensions[\"Service Type\"]) =~ \"API Management\"\n| extend Caller=coalesce(user_AuthenticatedId, user_Id, tostring(customDimensions[\"Subscription ID\"]), tostring(customDimensions[\"SubscriptionId\"]), tostring(customDimensions[\"subscriptionId\"]), client_IP, \"unknown\"), APIName=coalesce(tostring(customDimensions[\"API Name\"]), name), RequestOperation=coalesce(tostring(customDimensions[\"Operation Name\"]), name)\n| where \"{AgentSearch}\" == \"\" or Caller has \"{AgentSearch}\" or APIName has \"{AgentSearch}\" or RequestOperation has \"{AgentSearch}\"\n| distinct operation_Id;\nexceptions\n| extend RootType=coalesce(innermostType, type, outerType, \"unknown\"), ExceptionWeight=coalesce(tolong(itemCount), 1)\n| join kind=inner ApimOperations on operation_Id\n| summarize Exceptions=sum(ExceptionWeight), AffectedOperations=dcount(operation_Id) by bin(timestamp, 1h), RootType\n| order by timestamp asc",
              "size": 0,
              "visualization": "timechart",
              "title": "Correlated APIM exception volume by root type",
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.insights/components",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{APIMApplicationInsights}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "apim-exception-trend-appinsights",
            "conditionalVisibility": {
              "parameterName": "APIMTelemetrySource",
              "comparison": "isEqualTo",
              "value": "applicationInsights"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "#### Exception signatures and blast radius\n\nRanks the exception root types, problem IDs, and methods correlated with APIM operations. `AffectedRequests`, callers, APIs, result codes, first/last seen, and a sample message distinguish a noisy repeated stack from a broadly impactful fault. Exception messages can contain sensitive application data; apply the same access and export controls used for captured payloads."
            },
            "name": "apim-exception-hotspots-desc"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "let Requests=AppRequests\n| where SDKVersion startswith \"apim:\" or tostring(Properties[\"Service Type\"]) =~ \"API Management\"\n| extend Caller=coalesce(UserAuthenticatedId, UserId, tostring(Properties[\"Subscription ID\"]), tostring(Properties[\"SubscriptionId\"]), tostring(Properties[\"subscriptionId\"]), ClientIP, \"unknown\"), APIName=coalesce(tostring(Properties[\"API Name\"]), Name), RequestOperation=coalesce(tostring(Properties[\"Operation Name\"]), Name)\n| where \"{AgentSearch}\" == \"\" or Caller has \"{AgentSearch}\" or APIName has \"{AgentSearch}\" or RequestOperation has \"{AgentSearch}\"\n| summarize RequestTime=max(TimeGenerated), Caller=take_any(Caller), APIName=take_any(APIName), RequestOperation=take_any(RequestOperation), ResultCodes=make_set(ResultCode, 12) by OperationId;\nAppExceptions\n| extend RootType=coalesce(InnermostType, ExceptionType, OuterType, \"unknown\"), RootMessage=coalesce(InnermostMessage, Message, OuterMessage), RootMethod=coalesce(InnermostMethod, Method, OuterMethod, \"unknown\"), ExceptionWeight=coalesce(tolong(ItemCount), 1)\n| project ExceptionTime=TimeGenerated, OperationId, RootType, RootMessage, RootMethod, ProblemId, HandledAt, SeverityLevel, ExceptionWeight\n| join kind=inner Requests on OperationId\n| summarize Exceptions=sum(ExceptionWeight), AffectedRequests=dcount(OperationId), ImpactedCallers=dcountif(Caller, Caller != \"unknown\"), APIs=make_set(APIName, 10), Operations=make_set(RequestOperation, 20), ResultCodes=make_set(ResultCodes, 20), HandledLocations=make_set(HandledAt, 10), MaxSeverity=max(SeverityLevel), FirstSeen=min(ExceptionTime), LastSeen=max(ExceptionTime), SampleMessage=take_any(RootMessage) by RootType, ProblemId, RootMethod\n| top 30 by Exceptions desc",
              "size": 0,
              "title": "Exception hot spots and affected APIM callers",
              "gridSettings": {
                "formatters": [
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "Exceptions",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "red"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "AffectedRequests",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "yellow"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "ImpactedCallers",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "yellow"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{APIMWorkspace}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "apim-exception-hotspots",
            "conditionalVisibility": {
              "parameterName": "APIMTelemetrySource",
              "comparison": "isEqualTo",
              "value": "workspace"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "let Requests=requests\n| where sdkVersion startswith \"apim:\" or tostring(customDimensions[\"Service Type\"]) =~ \"API Management\"\n| extend Caller=coalesce(user_AuthenticatedId, user_Id, tostring(customDimensions[\"Subscription ID\"]), tostring(customDimensions[\"SubscriptionId\"]), tostring(customDimensions[\"subscriptionId\"]), client_IP, \"unknown\"), APIName=coalesce(tostring(customDimensions[\"API Name\"]), name), RequestOperation=coalesce(tostring(customDimensions[\"Operation Name\"]), name)\n| where \"{AgentSearch}\" == \"\" or Caller has \"{AgentSearch}\" or APIName has \"{AgentSearch}\" or RequestOperation has \"{AgentSearch}\"\n| summarize RequestTime=max(timestamp), Caller=take_any(Caller), APIName=take_any(APIName), RequestOperation=take_any(RequestOperation), ResultCodes=make_set(resultCode, 12) by operation_Id;\nexceptions\n| extend RootType=coalesce(innermostType, type, outerType, \"unknown\"), RootMessage=coalesce(innermostMessage, message, outerMessage), RootMethod=coalesce(innermostMethod, method, outerMethod, \"unknown\"), ExceptionWeight=coalesce(tolong(itemCount), 1)\n| project ExceptionTime=timestamp, operation_Id, RootType, RootMessage, RootMethod, problemId, handledAt, severityLevel, ExceptionWeight\n| join kind=inner Requests on operation_Id\n| summarize Exceptions=sum(ExceptionWeight), AffectedRequests=dcount(operation_Id), ImpactedCallers=dcountif(Caller, Caller != \"unknown\"), APIs=make_set(APIName, 10), Operations=make_set(RequestOperation, 20), ResultCodes=make_set(ResultCodes, 20), HandledLocations=make_set(handledAt, 10), MaxSeverity=max(severityLevel), FirstSeen=min(ExceptionTime), LastSeen=max(ExceptionTime), SampleMessage=take_any(RootMessage) by RootType, problemId, RootMethod\n| top 30 by Exceptions desc",
              "size": 0,
              "title": "Exception hot spots and affected APIM callers",
              "gridSettings": {
                "formatters": [
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "Exceptions",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "red"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "AffectedRequests",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "yellow"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "ImpactedCallers",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "yellow"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.insights/components",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{APIMApplicationInsights}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "apim-exception-hotspots-appinsights",
            "conditionalVisibility": {
              "parameterName": "APIMTelemetrySource",
              "comparison": "isEqualTo",
              "value": "applicationInsights"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "#### Timeout, cancellation, and deadline failures\n\nCombines timeout-like HTTP results (`408`, `499`, `504`) with correlated exception text such as timeout, deadline exceeded, task cancellation, and operation cancellation. Use the class, route, latency, exception type, and caller impact to separate caller disconnects from gateway/backend deadlines. Cancellation text is heuristic and should be validated against application behavior."
            },
            "name": "apim-timeout-diagnostics-desc"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "let Requests=AppRequests\n| where SDKVersion startswith \"apim:\" or tostring(Properties[\"Service Type\"]) =~ \"API Management\"\n| extend Caller=coalesce(UserAuthenticatedId, UserId, tostring(Properties[\"Subscription ID\"]), tostring(Properties[\"SubscriptionId\"]), tostring(Properties[\"subscriptionId\"]), ClientIP, \"unknown\"), APIName=coalesce(tostring(Properties[\"API Name\"]), Name), RequestOperation=coalesce(tostring(Properties[\"Operation Name\"]), Name), RequestWeight=coalesce(tolong(ItemCount), 1)\n| where \"{AgentSearch}\" == \"\" or Caller has \"{AgentSearch}\" or APIName has \"{AgentSearch}\" or RequestOperation has \"{AgentSearch}\"\n| project RequestTime=TimeGenerated, OperationId, Caller, APIName, RequestOperation, ResultCode, DurationMs, RequestWeight;\nlet Exceptions=AppExceptions\n| extend RootType=coalesce(InnermostType, ExceptionType, OuterType, \"unknown\"), RootMessage=coalesce(InnermostMessage, Message, OuterMessage)\n| summarize ExceptionTypes=make_set(RootType, 10), ProblemIds=make_set(ProblemId, 10), SampleException=take_any(RootMessage) by OperationId;\nRequests\n| join kind=leftouter Exceptions on OperationId\n| extend ExceptionSearch=tolower(strcat(strcat_array(ExceptionTypes, \" \"), \" \", coalesce(SampleException, \"\"))), Code=toint(ResultCode)\n| where Code in (408, 499, 504) or ExceptionSearch has_any (\"timeout\", \"timed out\", \"deadline exceeded\", \"taskcanceled\", \"task canceled\", \"operationcanceled\", \"operation canceled\")\n| extend TimeoutClass=case(Code == 408, \"Request timeout (408)\", Code == 499, \"Caller canceled or disconnected (499)\", Code == 504, \"Gateway or backend timeout (504)\", ExceptionSearch has \"deadline\", \"Deadline exceeded\", ExceptionSearch has_any (\"taskcanceled\", \"task canceled\", \"operationcanceled\", \"operation canceled\"), \"Cancellation exception\", \"Timeout exception\")\n| summarize Events=sum(RequestWeight), ImpactedCallers=dcountif(Caller, Caller != \"unknown\"), AvgMs=round(avg(DurationMs), 0), P95Ms=round(percentile(DurationMs, 95), 0), ResultCodes=make_set(ResultCode, 10), ExceptionTypes=take_any(ExceptionTypes), ProblemIds=take_any(ProblemIds), FirstSeen=min(RequestTime), LastSeen=max(RequestTime), SampleException=take_any(SampleException) by TimeoutClass, APIName, RequestOperation\n| top 50 by Events desc",
              "size": 0,
              "title": "Timeout and deadline failure concentration",
              "gridSettings": {
                "formatters": [
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "Events",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "red"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "P95Ms",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "yellow"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{APIMWorkspace}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "apim-timeout-diagnostics",
            "conditionalVisibility": {
              "parameterName": "APIMTelemetrySource",
              "comparison": "isEqualTo",
              "value": "workspace"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "let Requests=requests\n| where sdkVersion startswith \"apim:\" or tostring(customDimensions[\"Service Type\"]) =~ \"API Management\"\n| extend Caller=coalesce(user_AuthenticatedId, user_Id, tostring(customDimensions[\"Subscription ID\"]), tostring(customDimensions[\"SubscriptionId\"]), tostring(customDimensions[\"subscriptionId\"]), client_IP, \"unknown\"), APIName=coalesce(tostring(customDimensions[\"API Name\"]), name), RequestOperation=coalesce(tostring(customDimensions[\"Operation Name\"]), name), RequestWeight=coalesce(tolong(itemCount), 1)\n| where \"{AgentSearch}\" == \"\" or Caller has \"{AgentSearch}\" or APIName has \"{AgentSearch}\" or RequestOperation has \"{AgentSearch}\"\n| project RequestTime=timestamp, operation_Id, Caller, APIName, RequestOperation, resultCode, duration, RequestWeight;\nlet Exceptions=exceptions\n| extend RootType=coalesce(innermostType, type, outerType, \"unknown\"), RootMessage=coalesce(innermostMessage, message, outerMessage)\n| summarize ExceptionTypes=make_set(RootType, 10), ProblemIds=make_set(problemId, 10), SampleException=take_any(RootMessage) by operation_Id;\nRequests\n| join kind=leftouter Exceptions on operation_Id\n| extend ExceptionSearch=tolower(strcat(strcat_array(ExceptionTypes, \" \"), \" \", coalesce(SampleException, \"\"))), Code=toint(resultCode)\n| where Code in (408, 499, 504) or ExceptionSearch has_any (\"timeout\", \"timed out\", \"deadline exceeded\", \"taskcanceled\", \"task canceled\", \"operationcanceled\", \"operation canceled\")\n| extend TimeoutClass=case(Code == 408, \"Request timeout (408)\", Code == 499, \"Caller canceled or disconnected (499)\", Code == 504, \"Gateway or backend timeout (504)\", ExceptionSearch has \"deadline\", \"Deadline exceeded\", ExceptionSearch has_any (\"taskcanceled\", \"task canceled\", \"operationcanceled\", \"operation canceled\"), \"Cancellation exception\", \"Timeout exception\")\n| summarize Events=sum(RequestWeight), ImpactedCallers=dcountif(Caller, Caller != \"unknown\"), AvgMs=round(avg(duration), 0), P95Ms=round(percentile(duration, 95), 0), ResultCodes=make_set(resultCode, 10), ExceptionTypes=take_any(ExceptionTypes), ProblemIds=take_any(ProblemIds), FirstSeen=min(RequestTime), LastSeen=max(RequestTime), SampleException=take_any(SampleException) by TimeoutClass, APIName, RequestOperation\n| top 50 by Events desc",
              "size": 0,
              "title": "Timeout and deadline failure concentration",
              "gridSettings": {
                "formatters": [
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "Events",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "red"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "P95Ms",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "yellow"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.insights/components",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{APIMApplicationInsights}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "apim-timeout-diagnostics-appinsights",
            "conditionalVisibility": {
              "parameterName": "APIMTelemetrySource",
              "comparison": "isEqualTo",
              "value": "applicationInsights"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "#### Release and instance regression isolation\n\nGroups correlated exceptions by the emitting application role, version, and instance. Concentration in one version suggests a release regression; concentration in one instance suggests unhealthy or divergent infrastructure. Empty version values mean the emitting service did not stamp `AppVersion`, so use role and instance plus deployment records."
            },
            "name": "apim-exception-deployment-desc"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "let Requests=AppRequests\n| where SDKVersion startswith \"apim:\" or tostring(Properties[\"Service Type\"]) =~ \"API Management\"\n| extend Caller=coalesce(UserAuthenticatedId, UserId, tostring(Properties[\"Subscription ID\"]), tostring(Properties[\"SubscriptionId\"]), tostring(Properties[\"subscriptionId\"]), ClientIP, \"unknown\"), APIName=coalesce(tostring(Properties[\"API Name\"]), Name), RequestOperation=coalesce(tostring(Properties[\"Operation Name\"]), Name)\n| where \"{AgentSearch}\" == \"\" or Caller has \"{AgentSearch}\" or APIName has \"{AgentSearch}\" or RequestOperation has \"{AgentSearch}\"\n| summarize Caller=take_any(Caller), APIName=take_any(APIName), RequestOperation=take_any(RequestOperation) by OperationId;\nAppExceptions\n| extend RootType=coalesce(InnermostType, ExceptionType, OuterType, \"unknown\"), ExceptionWeight=coalesce(tolong(ItemCount), 1), Role=coalesce(AppRoleName, \"not stamped\"), Version=coalesce(AppVersion, \"not stamped\"), Instance=coalesce(AppRoleInstance, \"not stamped\")\n| join kind=inner Requests on OperationId\n| summarize Exceptions=sum(ExceptionWeight), AffectedRequests=dcount(OperationId), ImpactedCallers=dcountif(Caller, Caller != \"unknown\"), ExceptionTypes=make_set(RootType, 15), ProblemIds=make_set(ProblemId, 15), APIs=make_set(APIName, 10), Operations=make_set(RequestOperation, 20), FirstSeen=min(TimeGenerated), LastSeen=max(TimeGenerated) by Role, Version, Instance\n| top 50 by Exceptions desc",
              "size": 0,
              "title": "Exception impact by application version and instance",
              "gridSettings": {
                "formatters": [
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "Exceptions",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "red"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "AffectedRequests",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "yellow"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{APIMWorkspace}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "apim-exception-deployment",
            "conditionalVisibility": {
              "parameterName": "APIMTelemetrySource",
              "comparison": "isEqualTo",
              "value": "workspace"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "let Requests=requests\n| where sdkVersion startswith \"apim:\" or tostring(customDimensions[\"Service Type\"]) =~ \"API Management\"\n| extend Caller=coalesce(user_AuthenticatedId, user_Id, tostring(customDimensions[\"Subscription ID\"]), tostring(customDimensions[\"SubscriptionId\"]), tostring(customDimensions[\"subscriptionId\"]), client_IP, \"unknown\"), APIName=coalesce(tostring(customDimensions[\"API Name\"]), name), RequestOperation=coalesce(tostring(customDimensions[\"Operation Name\"]), name)\n| where \"{AgentSearch}\" == \"\" or Caller has \"{AgentSearch}\" or APIName has \"{AgentSearch}\" or RequestOperation has \"{AgentSearch}\"\n| summarize Caller=take_any(Caller), APIName=take_any(APIName), RequestOperation=take_any(RequestOperation) by operation_Id;\nexceptions\n| extend RootType=coalesce(innermostType, type, outerType, \"unknown\"), ExceptionWeight=coalesce(tolong(itemCount), 1), Role=coalesce(cloud_RoleName, \"not stamped\"), Version=coalesce(application_Version, \"not stamped\"), Instance=coalesce(cloud_RoleInstance, \"not stamped\")\n| join kind=inner Requests on operation_Id\n| summarize Exceptions=sum(ExceptionWeight), AffectedRequests=dcount(operation_Id), ImpactedCallers=dcountif(Caller, Caller != \"unknown\"), ExceptionTypes=make_set(RootType, 15), ProblemIds=make_set(problemId, 15), APIs=make_set(APIName, 10), Operations=make_set(RequestOperation, 20), FirstSeen=min(timestamp), LastSeen=max(timestamp) by Role, Version, Instance\n| top 50 by Exceptions desc",
              "size": 0,
              "title": "Exception impact by application version and instance",
              "gridSettings": {
                "formatters": [
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "Exceptions",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "red"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "AffectedRequests",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "yellow"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.insights/components",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{APIMApplicationInsights}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "apim-exception-deployment-appinsights",
            "conditionalVisibility": {
              "parameterName": "APIMTelemetrySource",
              "comparison": "isEqualTo",
              "value": "applicationInsights"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "#### Failure-to-exception diagnostic coverage\n\nMeasures which failed APIM requests have at least one `AppExceptions` record sharing `OperationId`. High `WithoutException` counts can be legitimate policy rejections (`4xx`), but for unexpected `5xx` failures they often indicate missing exception instrumentation, sampling mismatch, separate Application Insights resources, or lost trace context. This is telemetry coverage, not an application-health score."
            },
            "name": "apim-exception-coverage-desc"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "let ExceptionOperations=AppExceptions\n| summarize ExceptionCount=sum(coalesce(tolong(ItemCount), 1)), ExceptionTypes=make_set(coalesce(InnermostType, ExceptionType, OuterType, \"unknown\"), 20) by OperationId;\nAppRequests\n| where SDKVersion startswith \"apim:\" or tostring(Properties[\"Service Type\"]) =~ \"API Management\"\n| where Success == false or toint(ResultCode) >= 400\n| extend Caller=coalesce(UserAuthenticatedId, UserId, tostring(Properties[\"Subscription ID\"]), tostring(Properties[\"SubscriptionId\"]), tostring(Properties[\"subscriptionId\"]), ClientIP, \"unknown\"), APIName=coalesce(tostring(Properties[\"API Name\"]), Name), RequestOperation=coalesce(tostring(Properties[\"Operation Name\"]), Name), RequestWeight=coalesce(tolong(ItemCount), 1)\n| where \"{AgentSearch}\" == \"\" or Caller has \"{AgentSearch}\" or APIName has \"{AgentSearch}\" or RequestOperation has \"{AgentSearch}\"\n| join kind=leftouter ExceptionOperations on OperationId\n| extend HasException=isnotnull(ExceptionCount)\n| summarize FailedRequests=sum(RequestWeight), WithException=sum(iff(HasException, RequestWeight, 0)), WithoutException=sum(iff(HasException, 0, RequestWeight)), CorrelatedExceptions=sum(coalesce(ExceptionCount, 0)), ImpactedCallers=dcountif(Caller, Caller != \"unknown\"), ExceptionTypes=make_set(ExceptionTypes, 20), LastSeen=max(TimeGenerated) by APIName, RequestOperation, ResultCode\n| extend ExceptionCoveragePct=round(100.0 * todouble(WithException) / max_of(todouble(FailedRequests), 1.0), 1)\n| project APIName, RequestOperation, ResultCode, FailedRequests, WithException, WithoutException, ExceptionCoveragePct, CorrelatedExceptions, ImpactedCallers, ExceptionTypes, LastSeen\n| top 50 by FailedRequests desc",
              "size": 0,
              "title": "Failed requests with and without exception evidence",
              "gridSettings": {
                "formatters": [
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "WithoutException",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "red"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "ExceptionCoveragePct",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "yellow"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{APIMWorkspace}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "apim-exception-coverage",
            "conditionalVisibility": {
              "parameterName": "APIMTelemetrySource",
              "comparison": "isEqualTo",
              "value": "workspace"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "let ExceptionOperations=exceptions\n| summarize ExceptionCount=sum(coalesce(tolong(itemCount), 1)), ExceptionTypes=make_set(coalesce(innermostType, type, outerType, \"unknown\"), 20) by operation_Id;\nrequests\n| where sdkVersion startswith \"apim:\" or tostring(customDimensions[\"Service Type\"]) =~ \"API Management\"\n| where success == false or toint(resultCode) >= 400\n| extend Caller=coalesce(user_AuthenticatedId, user_Id, tostring(customDimensions[\"Subscription ID\"]), tostring(customDimensions[\"SubscriptionId\"]), tostring(customDimensions[\"subscriptionId\"]), client_IP, \"unknown\"), APIName=coalesce(tostring(customDimensions[\"API Name\"]), name), RequestOperation=coalesce(tostring(customDimensions[\"Operation Name\"]), name), RequestWeight=coalesce(tolong(itemCount), 1)\n| where \"{AgentSearch}\" == \"\" or Caller has \"{AgentSearch}\" or APIName has \"{AgentSearch}\" or RequestOperation has \"{AgentSearch}\"\n| join kind=leftouter ExceptionOperations on operation_Id\n| extend HasException=isnotnull(ExceptionCount)\n| summarize FailedRequests=sum(RequestWeight), WithException=sum(iff(HasException, RequestWeight, 0)), WithoutException=sum(iff(HasException, 0, RequestWeight)), CorrelatedExceptions=sum(coalesce(ExceptionCount, 0)), ImpactedCallers=dcountif(Caller, Caller != \"unknown\"), ExceptionTypes=make_set(ExceptionTypes, 20), LastSeen=max(timestamp) by APIName, RequestOperation, resultCode\n| extend ExceptionCoveragePct=round(100.0 * todouble(WithException) / max_of(todouble(FailedRequests), 1.0), 1)\n| project APIName, RequestOperation, resultCode, FailedRequests, WithException, WithoutException, ExceptionCoveragePct, CorrelatedExceptions, ImpactedCallers, ExceptionTypes, LastSeen\n| top 50 by FailedRequests desc",
              "size": 0,
              "title": "Failed requests with and without exception evidence",
              "gridSettings": {
                "formatters": [
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "WithoutException",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "red"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "ExceptionCoveragePct",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "yellow"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.insights/components",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{APIMApplicationInsights}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "apim-exception-coverage-appinsights",
            "conditionalVisibility": {
              "parameterName": "APIMTelemetrySource",
              "comparison": "isEqualTo",
              "value": "applicationInsights"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "### 🧠 LLM tokens and agent-aware correlation\n\nThese panels add AI consumption and semantic agent context to APIM's HTTP transaction view. Token metrics come from APIM policy instrumentation; agent/model/tool/conversation fields come from backend OpenTelemetry. W3C trace propagation is the bridge between the two layers."
            },
            "name": "apim-h3"
          },
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "#### LLM token consumption\n\nThe time series shows APIM custom token metrics by metric name and model/deployment dimension. Use it to investigate cost spikes, runaway loops, denial-of-wallet pressure, and uneven model usage. It requires custom metrics with dimensions plus `llm-emit-token-metric`; streaming providers can undercount when usage isn't returned or the stream terminates early. Missing metrics mean unavailable telemetry, not zero consumption."
            },
            "name": "apim-tokens-desc"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "AppMetrics\n| where Name has \"token\"\n| where SDKVersion startswith \"apim:\" or AppRoleName has \"apim\" or tostring(Properties) has \"API Management\"\n| extend Metric = Name, Model = coalesce(tostring(Properties[\"Model\"]), tostring(Properties[\"model\"]), tostring(Properties[\"Deployment\"]), \"not dimensioned\")\n| summarize Tokens = sum(Sum) by bin(TimeGenerated, 1h), Metric, Model\n| order by TimeGenerated asc",
              "size": 0,
              "visualization": "timechart",
              "title": "APIM LLM token custom metrics",
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{APIMWorkspace}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "apim-tokens",
            "conditionalVisibility": {
              "parameterName": "APIMTelemetrySource",
              "comparison": "isEqualTo",
              "value": "workspace"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "customMetrics\n| where name has \"token\"\n| where sdkVersion startswith \"apim:\" or cloud_RoleName has \"apim\" or tostring(customDimensions) has \"API Management\"\n| extend Metric = name, Model = coalesce(tostring(customDimensions[\"Model\"]), tostring(customDimensions[\"model\"]), tostring(customDimensions[\"Deployment\"]), \"not dimensioned\")\n| summarize Tokens = sum(valueSum) by bin(timestamp, 1h), Metric, Model\n| order by timestamp asc",
              "size": 0,
              "visualization": "timechart",
              "title": "APIM LLM token custom metrics",
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.insights/components",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{APIMApplicationInsights}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "apim-tokens-appinsights",
            "conditionalVisibility": {
              "parameterName": "APIMTelemetrySource",
              "comparison": "isEqualTo",
              "value": "applicationInsights"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "#### Gateway requests correlated with agent runs\n\nEach row joins one APIM request to backend GenAI spans sharing the same `OperationId`. It exposes the gateway result/latency beside agent, model, conversation, span count, tool calls, tokens, agent failures, and cumulative agent duration. Use the operation ID to reconstruct the end-to-end transaction. Duplicate or missing spans can occur when components use different Application Insights resources, sampling settings, or trace contexts."
            },
            "name": "apim-agent-correlation-desc"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "let Gateway = AppRequests\n| where SDKVersion startswith \"apim:\"\n| project GatewayTime = TimeGenerated, OperationId, GatewayOperation = Name, GatewayResult = ResultCode, GatewaySuccess = Success, GatewayMs = DurationMs;\nlet AgentSpans = AppDependencies\n| where isnotempty(tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.agent.name\"]))\n| summarize Agent = take_any(tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.agent.name\"])), Model = take_any(tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.request.model\"])), Conversation = take_any(tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.conversation.id\"])), AgentSpans = count(), ToolCalls = countif(isnotempty(tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.tool.name\"]))), InputTokens = sum(tolong(Properties[\"gen_ai.usage.input_tokens\"])), OutputTokens = sum(tolong(Properties[\"gen_ai.usage.output_tokens\"])), AgentFailures = countif(Success == false), AgentMs = round(sum(DurationMs), 0) by OperationId;\nGateway\n| join kind=inner AgentSpans on OperationId\n| where \"{AgentSearch}\" == \"\" or Agent has \"{AgentSearch}\" or Model has \"{AgentSearch}\" or GatewayOperation has \"{AgentSearch}\"\n| project GatewayTime, OperationId, GatewayOperation, GatewayResult, GatewaySuccess, GatewayMs, Agent, Model, Conversation, AgentSpans, ToolCalls, InputTokens, OutputTokens, AgentFailures, AgentMs\n| order by GatewayTime desc\n| take 100",
              "size": 0,
              "title": "Gateway operations correlated with agent runs",
              "gridSettings": {
                "formatters": [
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "GatewayMs",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "yellow"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "AgentFailures",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "red"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "InputTokens",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "purple"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "OutputTokens",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "purple"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{APIMWorkspace}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "apim-agent-correlation",
            "conditionalVisibility": {
              "parameterName": "APIMTelemetrySource",
              "comparison": "isEqualTo",
              "value": "workspace"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "let Gateway = requests\n| where sdkVersion startswith \"apim:\"\n| project GatewayTime = timestamp, operation_Id, GatewayOperation = name, GatewayResult = resultCode, GatewaySuccess = success, GatewayMs = duration;\nlet AgentSpans = dependencies\n| where isnotempty(tostring(customDimensions[\"gen_ai.agent.name\"]))\n| summarize Agent = take_any(tostring(customDimensions[\"gen_ai.agent.name\"])), Model = take_any(tostring(customDimensions[\"gen_ai.request.model\"])), Conversation = take_any(tostring(customDimensions[\"gen_ai.conversation.id\"])), AgentSpans = count(), ToolCalls = countif(isnotempty(tostring(customDimensions[\"gen_ai.tool.name\"]))), InputTokens = sum(tolong(customDimensions[\"gen_ai.usage.input_tokens\"])), OutputTokens = sum(tolong(customDimensions[\"gen_ai.usage.output_tokens\"])), AgentFailures = countif(success == false), AgentMs = round(sum(duration), 0) by operation_Id;\nGateway\n| join kind=inner AgentSpans on operation_Id\n| where \"{AgentSearch}\" == \"\" or Agent has \"{AgentSearch}\" or Model has \"{AgentSearch}\" or GatewayOperation has \"{AgentSearch}\"\n| project GatewayTime, operation_Id, GatewayOperation, GatewayResult, GatewaySuccess, GatewayMs, Agent, Model, Conversation, AgentSpans, ToolCalls, InputTokens, OutputTokens, AgentFailures, AgentMs\n| order by GatewayTime desc\n| take 100",
              "size": 0,
              "title": "Gateway operations correlated with agent runs",
              "gridSettings": {
                "formatters": [
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "GatewayMs",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "yellow"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "AgentFailures",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "red"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "InputTokens",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "purple"
                    }
                  },
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "OutputTokens",
                    "formatter": 4,
                    "formatOptions": {
                      "palette": "purple"
                    }
                  }
                ]
              },
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.insights/components",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{APIMApplicationInsights}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "apim-agent-correlation-appinsights",
            "conditionalVisibility": {
              "parameterName": "APIMTelemetrySource",
              "comparison": "isEqualTo",
              "value": "applicationInsights"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "#### W3C trace-correlation coverage\n\nCoverage compares distinct APIM operations with operations that also contain an agent span. A low percentage means `traceparent` may not be propagated, the agent backend isn't instrumented, telemetry is exported elsewhere, or sampling differs between layers. Not every APIM API is necessarily an agent API, so scope or interpret the percentage against the APIs expected to produce GenAI spans."
            },
            "name": "apim-correlation-coverage-desc"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "let Gateway = AppRequests\n| where SDKVersion startswith \"apim:\"\n| summarize GatewayRequests = count(), GatewayOperations = dcount(OperationId);\nlet Correlated = AppRequests\n| where SDKVersion startswith \"apim:\"\n| join kind=inner (AppDependencies | where isnotempty(tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.agent.name\"])) | distinct OperationId) on OperationId\n| summarize CorrelatedRequests = count(), CorrelatedOperations = dcount(OperationId);\nGateway\n| extend JoinKey = 1\n| join kind=fullouter (Correlated | extend JoinKey = 1) on JoinKey\n| project GatewayRequests = coalesce(GatewayRequests, 0), GatewayOperations = coalesce(GatewayOperations, 0), CorrelatedRequests = coalesce(CorrelatedRequests, 0), CorrelatedOperations = coalesce(CorrelatedOperations, 0)\n| extend CorrelationPct = iff(GatewayOperations == 0, 0.0, round(100.0 * CorrelatedOperations / GatewayOperations, 2)), Guidance = iff(CorrelatedOperations == 0, \"Enable W3C correlation and propagate traceparent to the instrumented agent backend\", \"APIM and agent spans share OperationId\")",
              "size": 0,
              "title": "W3C trace correlation coverage",
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{APIMWorkspace}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "apim-correlation-coverage",
            "conditionalVisibility": {
              "parameterName": "APIMTelemetrySource",
              "comparison": "isEqualTo",
              "value": "workspace"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "let Gateway = requests\n| where sdkVersion startswith \"apim:\"\n| summarize GatewayRequests = count(), GatewayOperations = dcount(operation_Id);\nlet Correlated = requests\n| where sdkVersion startswith \"apim:\"\n| join kind=inner (dependencies | where isnotempty(tostring(customDimensions[\"gen_ai.agent.name\"])) | distinct operation_Id) on operation_Id\n| summarize CorrelatedRequests = count(), CorrelatedOperations = dcount(operation_Id);\nGateway\n| extend JoinKey = 1\n| join kind=fullouter (Correlated | extend JoinKey = 1) on JoinKey\n| project GatewayRequests = coalesce(GatewayRequests, 0), GatewayOperations = coalesce(GatewayOperations, 0), CorrelatedRequests = coalesce(CorrelatedRequests, 0), CorrelatedOperations = coalesce(CorrelatedOperations, 0)\n| extend CorrelationPct = iff(GatewayOperations == 0, 0.0, round(100.0 * CorrelatedOperations / GatewayOperations, 2)), Guidance = iff(CorrelatedOperations == 0, \"Enable W3C correlation and propagate traceparent to the instrumented agent backend\", \"APIM and agent spans share OperationId\")",
              "size": 0,
              "title": "W3C trace correlation coverage",
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.insights/components",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{APIMApplicationInsights}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "apim-correlation-coverage-appinsights",
            "conditionalVisibility": {
              "parameterName": "APIMTelemetrySource",
              "comparison": "isEqualTo",
              "value": "applicationInsights"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "#### Telemetry-source health\n\nThis checklist confirms whether APIM frontend requests, backend dependencies, exceptions, policy traces, token metrics, agent GenAI spans, and protected GenAI content are arriving in the selected range. Use `LastSeen` to detect stale pipelines and `Records` only as an availability indicator. A zero can be expected when a feature isn't configured or no matching event occurred; it isn't proof that the control is healthy."
            },
            "name": "apim-health-desc"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "union isfuzzy=true\n(AppRequests | where SDKVersion startswith \"apim:\" | summarize Records = count(), LastSeen = max(TimeGenerated) | extend Signal = \"APIM frontend requests\"),\n(AppDependencies | where SDKVersion startswith \"apim:\" | summarize Records = count(), LastSeen = max(TimeGenerated) | extend Signal = \"APIM backend dependencies\"),\n(AppExceptions | where SDKVersion startswith \"apim:\" | summarize Records = count(), LastSeen = max(TimeGenerated) | extend Signal = \"APIM exceptions\"),\n(AppTraces | where SDKVersion startswith \"apim:\" | summarize Records = count(), LastSeen = max(TimeGenerated) | extend Signal = \"APIM policy traces\"),\n(AppMetrics | where Name has \"token\" and (SDKVersion startswith \"apim:\" or AppRoleName has \"apim\" or tostring(Properties) has \"API Management\") | summarize Records = count(), LastSeen = max(TimeGenerated) | extend Signal = \"APIM token metrics\"),\n(AppDependencies | where isnotempty(tostring(Properties[\"gen_ai.agent.name\"])) | summarize Records = count(), LastSeen = max(TimeGenerated) | extend Signal = \"Agent OTel GenAI spans\"),\n(AppGenAIContent | summarize Records = count(), LastSeen = max(TimeGenerated) | extend Signal = \"Agent OTel GenAI content (protected)\")\n| project Signal, Records, LastSeen, Status = iff(Records > 0, \"Available\", \"No data in selected range\")\n| order by Signal asc",
              "size": 0,
              "title": "APIM and agent telemetry health",
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{APIMWorkspace}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "apim-health",
            "conditionalVisibility": {
              "parameterName": "APIMTelemetrySource",
              "comparison": "isEqualTo",
              "value": "workspace"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "union isfuzzy=true\n(requests | where sdkVersion startswith \"apim:\" | summarize Records = count(), LastSeen = max(timestamp) | extend Signal = \"APIM frontend requests\"),\n(dependencies | where sdkVersion startswith \"apim:\" | summarize Records = count(), LastSeen = max(timestamp) | extend Signal = \"APIM backend dependencies\"),\n(exceptions | where sdkVersion startswith \"apim:\" | summarize Records = count(), LastSeen = max(timestamp) | extend Signal = \"APIM exceptions\"),\n(traces | where sdkVersion startswith \"apim:\" | summarize Records = count(), LastSeen = max(timestamp) | extend Signal = \"APIM policy traces\"),\n(customMetrics | where name has \"token\" and (sdkVersion startswith \"apim:\" or cloud_RoleName has \"apim\" or tostring(customDimensions) has \"API Management\") | summarize Records = count(), LastSeen = max(timestamp) | extend Signal = \"APIM token metrics\"),\n(dependencies | where isnotempty(tostring(customDimensions[\"gen_ai.agent.name\"])) | summarize Records = count(), LastSeen = max(timestamp) | extend Signal = \"Agent OTel GenAI spans\"),\n(genAIContent | summarize Records = count(), LastSeen = max(timestamp) | extend Signal = \"Agent OTel GenAI content (protected)\")\n| project Signal, Records, LastSeen, Status = iff(Records > 0, \"Available\", \"No data in selected range\")\n| order by Signal asc",
              "size": 0,
              "title": "APIM and agent telemetry health",
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.insights/components",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{APIMApplicationInsights}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "apim-health-appinsights",
            "conditionalVisibility": {
              "parameterName": "APIMTelemetrySource",
              "comparison": "isEqualTo",
              "value": "applicationInsights"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "### 🔎 AppRequests payload security — input, instructions, tools, request & response bodies\n\nThese panels intentionally display captured APIM payload fields. In Application Insights resource scope the table is `requests` and the property bag is `customDimensions`; in a linked Log Analytics workspace the equivalents are `AppRequests` and `Properties`. `Request-Body` is parsed into `Input`, `Instructions`, `Model`, and `Tools`, while the complete `RequestBody` and `ResponseBody` remain visible. This evidence can contain credentials, personal data, prompts, system instructions, and tool schemas; restrict workbook access, retention, export, screenshots, and incident access accordingly.",
              "style": "warning"
            },
            "name": "apim-payload-h"
          },
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "#### Payload capture coverage\n\nShows how many APIM request rows contain request and response bodies. Low coverage makes body-driven detections incomplete; high coverage materially increases sensitive-data exposure and ingestion cost. APIM rows are identified by the current `apim:` SDK signature or `Service Type == API Management`."
            },
            "name": "apim-payload-coverage-desc"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "AppRequests\n| where SDKVersion startswith \"apim:\" or tostring(Properties[\"Service Type\"]) =~ \"API Management\"\n| extend RequestBody = tostring(Properties[\"Request-Body\"]), ResponseBody = tostring(Properties[\"Response-Body\"])\n| summarize Total = count(), WithRequestBody = countif(isnotempty(RequestBody)), WithResponseBody = countif(isnotempty(ResponseBody)), WithBoth = countif(isnotempty(RequestBody) and isnotempty(ResponseBody))\n| extend RequestBodyPct = iff(Total == 0, 0.0, round(100.0 * WithRequestBody / Total, 1)), ResponseBodyPct = iff(Total == 0, 0.0, round(100.0 * WithResponseBody / Total, 1))\n| project Total, WithRequestBody, RequestBodyPct, WithResponseBody, ResponseBodyPct, WithBoth",
              "size": 0,
              "title": "AppRequests payload logging coverage",
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{APIMWorkspace}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "apim-payload-coverage",
            "conditionalVisibility": {
              "parameterName": "APIMTelemetrySource",
              "comparison": "isEqualTo",
              "value": "workspace"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "requests\n| where sdkVersion startswith \"apim:\" or tostring(customDimensions[\"Service Type\"]) =~ \"API Management\"\n| extend RequestBody = tostring(customDimensions[\"Request-Body\"]), ResponseBody = tostring(customDimensions[\"Response-Body\"])\n| summarize Total = count(), WithRequestBody = countif(isnotempty(RequestBody)), WithResponseBody = countif(isnotempty(ResponseBody)), WithBoth = countif(isnotempty(RequestBody) and isnotempty(ResponseBody))\n| extend RequestBodyPct = iff(Total == 0, 0.0, round(100.0 * WithRequestBody / Total, 1)), ResponseBodyPct = iff(Total == 0, 0.0, round(100.0 * WithResponseBody / Total, 1))\n| project Total, WithRequestBody, RequestBodyPct, WithResponseBody, ResponseBodyPct, WithBoth",
              "size": 0,
              "title": "AppRequests payload logging coverage",
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.insights/components",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{APIMApplicationInsights}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "apim-payload-coverage-appinsights",
            "conditionalVisibility": {
              "parameterName": "APIMTelemetrySource",
              "comparison": "isEqualTo",
              "value": "applicationInsights"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "#### Full request and response body investigation\n\nDisplays complete captured bodies plus parsed input, instructions, model, tools, route, result, request ID, and operation ID. Use `OperationId` to correlate with dependencies, traces, and agent spans. Rows with no captured body are excluded."
            },
            "name": "apim-body-events-desc"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "AppRequests\n| where SDKVersion startswith \"apim:\" or tostring(Properties[\"Service Type\"]) =~ \"API Management\"\n| extend RequestBody = tostring(Properties[\"Request-Body\"]), ResponseBody = tostring(Properties[\"Response-Body\"])\n| where isnotempty(RequestBody) or isnotempty(ResponseBody)\n| extend RequestJson = parse_json(RequestBody), ResponseJson = parse_json(ResponseBody)\n| extend Input = tostring(RequestJson.input), Instructions = tostring(RequestJson.instructions), Model = tostring(RequestJson.model), Tools = tostring(RequestJson.tools), ToolChoice = tostring(RequestJson.tool_choice), Stream = tostring(RequestJson.stream), PolicyStatus = tostring(ResponseJson.statusCode), PolicyMessage = tostring(ResponseJson.message), HTTPMethod = tostring(Properties[\"HTTP Method\"]), APIName = tostring(Properties[\"API Name\"]), OperationName = tostring(Properties[\"Operation Name\"]), RequestId = tostring(Properties[\"Request Id\"]), ServiceName = tostring(Properties[\"Service Name\"]), Region = tostring(Properties[\"Region\"]), Caller = coalesce(UserAuthenticatedId, UserId, ClientIP, \"unknown\")\n| where \"{AgentSearch}\" == \"\" or Input has \"{AgentSearch}\" or Instructions has \"{AgentSearch}\" or Model has \"{AgentSearch}\" or Tools has \"{AgentSearch}\" or APIName has \"{AgentSearch}\" or Caller has \"{AgentSearch}\"\n| project TimeGenerated, Success, ResultCode, PolicyStatus, PolicyMessage, Caller, HTTPMethod, APIName, OperationName, Name, Url, Model, Stream, ToolChoice, Input, Instructions, Tools, RequestBody, ResponseBody, RequestId, OperationId, DurationMs, ServiceName, Region\n| order by TimeGenerated desc\n| take 250",
              "size": 0,
              "title": "APIM requests — full input, request body, and response body",
              "gridSettings": {
                "formatters": [
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "ResultCode",
                    "formatter": 0
                  },
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "Url",
                    "formatter": 1
                  }
                ]
              },
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{APIMWorkspace}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "apim-body-events",
            "conditionalVisibility": {
              "parameterName": "APIMTelemetrySource",
              "comparison": "isEqualTo",
              "value": "workspace"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "requests\n| where sdkVersion startswith \"apim:\" or tostring(customDimensions[\"Service Type\"]) =~ \"API Management\"\n| extend RequestBody = tostring(customDimensions[\"Request-Body\"]), ResponseBody = tostring(customDimensions[\"Response-Body\"])\n| where isnotempty(RequestBody) or isnotempty(ResponseBody)\n| extend RequestJson = parse_json(RequestBody), ResponseJson = parse_json(ResponseBody)\n| extend Input = tostring(RequestJson.input), Instructions = tostring(RequestJson.instructions), Model = tostring(RequestJson.model), Tools = tostring(RequestJson.tools), ToolChoice = tostring(RequestJson.tool_choice), Stream = tostring(RequestJson.stream), PolicyStatus = tostring(ResponseJson.statusCode), PolicyMessage = tostring(ResponseJson.message), HTTPMethod = tostring(customDimensions[\"HTTP Method\"]), APIName = tostring(customDimensions[\"API Name\"]), operation_Name = tostring(customDimensions[\"Operation Name\"]), RequestId = tostring(customDimensions[\"Request Id\"]), ServiceName = tostring(customDimensions[\"Service Name\"]), Region = tostring(customDimensions[\"Region\"]), Caller = coalesce(user_AuthenticatedId, user_Id, client_IP, \"unknown\")\n| where \"{AgentSearch}\" == \"\" or Input has \"{AgentSearch}\" or Instructions has \"{AgentSearch}\" or Model has \"{AgentSearch}\" or Tools has \"{AgentSearch}\" or APIName has \"{AgentSearch}\" or Caller has \"{AgentSearch}\"\n| project timestamp, success, resultCode, PolicyStatus, PolicyMessage, Caller, HTTPMethod, APIName, operation_Name, name, url, Model, Stream, ToolChoice, Input, Instructions, Tools, RequestBody, ResponseBody, RequestId, operation_Id, duration, ServiceName, Region\n| order by timestamp desc\n| take 250",
              "size": 0,
              "title": "APIM requests — full input, request body, and response body",
              "gridSettings": {
                "formatters": [
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "resultCode",
                    "formatter": 0
                  },
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "url",
                    "formatter": 1
                  }
                ]
              },
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.insights/components",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{APIMApplicationInsights}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "apim-body-events-appinsights",
            "conditionalVisibility": {
              "parameterName": "APIMTelemetrySource",
              "comparison": "isEqualTo",
              "value": "applicationInsights"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "#### Content-safety blocks from AppRequests\n\nConfirms content-safety enforcement by parsing the APIM `403` response message, then displays the full blocked input and body. It detects `Request failed content safety check.` without requiring `AppTraces`. Streaming response enforcement can terminate a stream without a normal `403`, so the trace panel remains complementary."
            },
            "name": "apim-request-safety-desc"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "AppRequests\n| where SDKVersion startswith \"apim:\" or tostring(Properties[\"Service Type\"]) =~ \"API Management\"\n| extend RequestBody = tostring(Properties[\"Request-Body\"]), ResponseBody = tostring(Properties[\"Response-Body\"]), RequestJson = parse_json(tostring(Properties[\"Request-Body\"])), ResponseJson = parse_json(tostring(Properties[\"Response-Body\"]))\n| extend PolicyMessage = coalesce(tostring(ResponseJson.message), ResponseBody), PolicyStatus = tostring(ResponseJson.statusCode)\n| where ResultCode == \"403\" and PolicyMessage has \"content safety\"\n| extend Input = tostring(RequestJson.input), Instructions = tostring(RequestJson.instructions), Model = tostring(RequestJson.model), Tools = tostring(RequestJson.tools), Caller = coalesce(UserAuthenticatedId, UserId, ClientIP, \"unknown\"), RequestId = tostring(Properties[\"Request Id\"]), APIName = tostring(Properties[\"API Name\"]), ServiceName = tostring(Properties[\"Service Name\"]), Region = tostring(Properties[\"Region\"])\n| project TimeGenerated, Signal = \"CONTENT SAFETY BLOCK\", Caller, ResultCode, PolicyStatus, PolicyMessage, APIName, Name, Url, Model, Input, Instructions, Tools, RequestBody, ResponseBody, RequestId, OperationId, DurationMs, ServiceName, Region\n| order by TimeGenerated desc\n| take 250",
              "size": 0,
              "title": "Content-safety blocked requests — full payload evidence",
              "gridSettings": {
                "formatters": [
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "Signal",
                    "formatter": 0
                  }
                ]
              },
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{APIMWorkspace}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "apim-request-safety",
            "conditionalVisibility": {
              "parameterName": "APIMTelemetrySource",
              "comparison": "isEqualTo",
              "value": "workspace"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "requests\n| where sdkVersion startswith \"apim:\" or tostring(customDimensions[\"Service Type\"]) =~ \"API Management\"\n| extend RequestBody = tostring(customDimensions[\"Request-Body\"]), ResponseBody = tostring(customDimensions[\"Response-Body\"]), RequestJson = parse_json(tostring(customDimensions[\"Request-Body\"])), ResponseJson = parse_json(tostring(customDimensions[\"Response-Body\"]))\n| extend PolicyMessage = coalesce(tostring(ResponseJson.message), ResponseBody), PolicyStatus = tostring(ResponseJson.statusCode)\n| where resultCode == \"403\" and PolicyMessage has \"content safety\"\n| extend Input = tostring(RequestJson.input), Instructions = tostring(RequestJson.instructions), Model = tostring(RequestJson.model), Tools = tostring(RequestJson.tools), Caller = coalesce(user_AuthenticatedId, user_Id, client_IP, \"unknown\"), RequestId = tostring(customDimensions[\"Request Id\"]), APIName = tostring(customDimensions[\"API Name\"]), ServiceName = tostring(customDimensions[\"Service Name\"]), Region = tostring(customDimensions[\"Region\"])\n| project timestamp, Signal = \"CONTENT SAFETY BLOCK\", Caller, resultCode, PolicyStatus, PolicyMessage, APIName, name, url, Model, Input, Instructions, Tools, RequestBody, ResponseBody, RequestId, operation_Id, duration, ServiceName, Region\n| order by timestamp desc\n| take 250",
              "size": 0,
              "title": "Content-safety blocked requests — full payload evidence",
              "gridSettings": {
                "formatters": [
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "Signal",
                    "formatter": 0
                  }
                ]
              },
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.insights/components",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{APIMApplicationInsights}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "apim-request-safety-appinsights",
            "conditionalVisibility": {
              "parameterName": "APIMTelemetrySource",
              "comparison": "isEqualTo",
              "value": "applicationInsights"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "#### Direct prompt-injection / jailbreak markers and outcome\n\nSearches parsed input and the complete request body for instruction override, system-prompt, role-change, and jailbreak markers. `ALLOWED / REVIEW` means APIM returned success despite a heuristic match; `BLOCKED` means a policy rejected it. Review full payload and caller context because security testing and quoted content can match."
            },
            "name": "apim-request-injection-desc"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "AppRequests\n| where SDKVersion startswith \"apim:\" or tostring(Properties[\"Service Type\"]) =~ \"API Management\"\n| extend RequestBody = tostring(Properties[\"Request-Body\"]), ResponseBody = tostring(Properties[\"Response-Body\"])\n| where isnotempty(RequestBody)\n| extend RequestJson = parse_json(RequestBody), ResponseJson = parse_json(ResponseBody)\n| extend Input = tostring(RequestJson.input), Instructions = tostring(RequestJson.instructions), Model = tostring(RequestJson.model), Tools = tostring(RequestJson.tools), Search = strcat(tostring(RequestJson.input), \" \", RequestBody)\n| where Search matches regex @\"(?i)(ignore (all|any|the|previous|prior|above).{0,40}instruction|disregard.{0,40}instruction|system prompt|developer mode|jailbreak|do anything now|you are now|act as.{0,30}(admin|administrator|system)|olvida.{0,40}instrucci)\"\n| extend Outcome = iff(Success == true or toint(ResultCode) between (200 .. 299), \"ALLOWED / REVIEW\", \"BLOCKED\"), Caller = coalesce(UserAuthenticatedId, UserId, ClientIP, \"unknown\"), PolicyMessage = tostring(ResponseJson.message), RequestId = tostring(Properties[\"Request Id\"]), APIName = tostring(Properties[\"API Name\"])\n| project TimeGenerated, Outcome, Caller, ResultCode, PolicyMessage, APIName, Name, Url, Model, Input, Instructions, Tools, RequestBody, ResponseBody, RequestId, OperationId, DurationMs\n| order by TimeGenerated desc\n| take 250",
              "size": 0,
              "title": "Prompt-injection patterns in APIM request bodies",
              "gridSettings": {
                "formatters": [
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "Outcome",
                    "formatter": 0
                  }
                ]
              },
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.operationalinsights/workspaces",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{APIMWorkspace}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "apim-request-injection",
            "conditionalVisibility": {
              "parameterName": "APIMTelemetrySource",
              "comparison": "isEqualTo",
              "value": "workspace"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "requests\n| where sdkVersion startswith \"apim:\" or tostring(customDimensions[\"Service Type\"]) =~ \"API Management\"\n| extend RequestBody = tostring(customDimensions[\"Request-Body\"]), ResponseBody = tostring(customDimensions[\"Response-Body\"])\n| where isnotempty(RequestBody)\n| extend RequestJson = parse_json(RequestBody), ResponseJson = parse_json(ResponseBody)\n| extend Input = tostring(RequestJson.input), Instructions = tostring(RequestJson.instructions), Model = tostring(RequestJson.model), Tools = tostring(RequestJson.tools), Search = strcat(tostring(RequestJson.input), \" \", RequestBody)\n| where Search matches regex @\"(?i)(ignore (all|any|the|previous|prior|above).{0,40}instruction|disregard.{0,40}instruction|system prompt|developer mode|jailbreak|do anything now|you are now|act as.{0,30}(admin|administrator|system)|olvida.{0,40}instrucci)\"\n| extend Outcome = iff(success == true or toint(resultCode) between (200 .. 299), \"ALLOWED / REVIEW\", \"BLOCKED\"), Caller = coalesce(user_AuthenticatedId, user_Id, client_IP, \"unknown\"), PolicyMessage = tostring(ResponseJson.message), RequestId = tostring(customDimensions[\"Request Id\"]), APIName = tostring(customDimensions[\"API Name\"])\n| project timestamp, Outcome, Caller, resultCode, PolicyMessage, APIName, name, url, Model, Input, Instructions, Tools, RequestBody, ResponseBody, RequestId, operation_Id, duration\n| order by timestamp desc\n| take 250",
              "size": 0,
              "title": "Prompt-injection patterns in APIM request bodies",
              "gridSettings": {
                "formatters": [
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "Outcome",
                    "formatter": 0
                  }
                ]
              },
              "queryType": 0,
              "resourceType": "microsoft.insights/components",
              "crossComponentResources": [
                "{APIMApplicationInsights}"
              ],
              "timeContextFromParameter": "TimeRange"
            },
            "name": "apim-request-injection-appinsights",
            "conditionalVisibility": {
              "parameterName": "APIMTelemetrySource",
              "comparison": "isEqualTo",
              "value": "applicationInsights"
            }
          },
          {
            "type": 1,
            "content": {
              "json": "#### Secrets and sensitive-data indicators in request bodies\n\nSearches captured payloads for AWS access keys, private-key blocks, JWT-like values, credential assignments, credit-card-like numbers, and bulk email addresses. Full matching bodies remain visible for investigation and must be handled as sensitive evidence."
            },
            "name": "apim-request-sensitive-desc"
          },
          {
            "type": 3,
            "content": {
              "version": "KqlItem/1.0",
              "query": "AppRequests\n| where SDKVersion startswith \"apim:\" or tostring(Properties[\"Service Type\"]) =~ \"API Management\"\n| extend RequestBody = tostring(Properties[\"Request-Body\"]), ResponseBody = tostring(Properties[\"Response-Body\"])\n| where isnotempty(RequestBody)\n| extend Input = tostring(parse_json(RequestBody).input), Instructions = tostring(parse_json(RequestBody).instructions), Model = tostring(parse_json(RequestBody).model)\n| extend HasAwsKey = RequestBody matches regex @\"AKIA[0-9A-Z]{16}\", HasPrivateKey = RequestBody contains \"-----BEGIN\" and RequestBody contains \"PRIVATE KEY-----\", HasJwt = RequestBody matches regex @\"eyJ[A-Za-z0-9_-]{10,}.[A-Za-z0-9_-]{10,}.[A-Za-z0-9_-]{10,}\", HasCredentialAssignment = RequestBody matches regex @\"(?i)(password|secret|connectionstring|connstring|api[_ -]?key)s*[:=]\", HasCreditCard = RequestBody matches regex @\"\b(?:d[ -]?){13,16}\b\", EmailCount = array_length(extract_all(@\"([A-Za-z0-9._%+-]+@[A-Za-z0-9.-]+.[A-Za-z]{2,})\", RequestBody))\n| where HasAwsKey or HasPrivateKey or HasJwt or HasCredentialAssignment or HasCreditCard or EmailCount >= 10\n| extend Signal = strcat(iff(HasAwsKey, \"AWSAccessKey;\", \"\"), iff(HasPrivateKey, \"PrivateKey;\", \"\"), iff(HasJwt, \"JWT;\", \"\"), iff(HasCredentialAssignment, \"CredentialAssignment;\", \"\"), iff(HasCreditCard, \"CreditCardLike;\", \"\"), iff(EmailCount >= 10, strcat(\"BulkEmails(\", tostring(EmailCount), \");\"), \"\")), Caller = coalesce(UserAuthenticatedId, UserId, ClientIP, \"unknown\"), RequestId = tostring(Properties[\"Request Id\"]), APIName = tostring(Properties[\"API Name\"])\n| project TimeGenerated, Signal, Caller, Success, ResultCode, APIName, Name, Url, Model, Input, Instructions, RequestBody, ResponseBody, EmailCount, RequestId, OperationId\n| order by TimeGenerated desc\n| take 250",
              "size": 0,
              "title": "Sensitive data indicators in APIM request bodies",
              "gridSettings": {
                "formatters": [
                  {
                    "columnMatch": "Signal",
                    "formatter": 0
                  }
                ]
              },
              "queryType": 0,
